1
00:01:16,457 --> 00:01:18,995
I believe in America.

2
00:01:19,335 --> 00:01:22,289
America has made my fortune.

3
00:01:22,505 --> 00:01:26,585
And I raised my daughter
in the American fashion.

4
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:31,712
I gave her freedom, but I taught her
never to dishonor her family.

5
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:35,922
She found a boyfriend, not an Italian.

6
00:01:36,185 --> 00:01:40,597
She went to the movies with him.
She stayed out late.

7
00:01:40,814 --> 00:01:43,270
I didn't protest.

8
00:01:43,484 --> 00:01:48,062
Two months ago he took her for a drive
with another boyfriend.

9
00:01:49,257 --> 00:01:51,878
They made her drink whiskey

10
00:01:52,034 --> 00:01:55,866
and then they tried to
take advantage of her.

11
00:01:56,445 --> 00:02:01,072
She resisted, she kept her honor.

12
00:02:01,877 --> 00:02:05,376
So they beat her like an animal.

13
00:02:06,719 --> 00:02:11,778
When I went to the hospital,
her nose was broken,

14
00:02:11,803 --> 00:02:16,595
her jaw was shattered,
held together by wire.

15
00:02:18,511 --> 00:02:21,454
She couldn't even weep
because of the pain.

16
00:02:23,992 --> 00:02:27,778
But I wept. Why did I weep?

17
00:02:30,170 --> 00:02:32,579
She was the light of my life.

18
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,226
Beautiful girl.

19
00:02:39,927 --> 00:02:42,480
Now she will never be beautiful again.

20
00:02:49,556 --> 00:02:51,177
Sorry.

21
00:02:59,014 --> 00:03:02,928
I went to the police,
like a good American.

22
00:03:03,827 --> 00:03:06,122
These two boys were brought to trial.

23
00:03:07,572 --> 00:03:12,128
The judge sentenced them to three years
in prison, but suspended the sentence.

24
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:19,201
Suspended the sentence!
They went free that very day!

25
00:03:21,054 --> 00:03:24,198
I stood in the courtroom like a fool.

26
00:03:24,416 --> 00:03:28,246
Those two bastards, they smiled at me.

27
00:03:29,129 --> 00:03:35,048
Then I said to my wife, "For justice,
we must go to Don Corleone."

28
00:03:40,131 --> 00:03:43,778
Why did you go to the police?
Why didn't you come to me first?

29
00:03:44,752 --> 00:03:49,894
What do you want of me? Tell me
anything, but do what I beg you to do.

30
00:03:50,847 --> 00:03:52,294
What is that?

31
00:04:02,723 --> 00:04:05,216
I want them dead.

32
00:04:17,163 --> 00:04:18,783
That I cannot do.

33
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,789
I'll give you anything you ask.

34
00:04:25,034 --> 00:04:30,354
I've known you many years, but this
is the first time you've asked for help.

35
00:04:31,704 --> 00:04:36,650
I can't remember the last time
you invited me for a cup of coffee.

36
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:41,190
Even though my wife is godmother
to your only child.

37
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:46,089
But let's be frank here.
You never wanted my friendship.

38
00:04:47,055 --> 00:04:50,589
And you were afraid to be in my debt.

39
00:04:50,913 --> 00:04:53,370
I didn't want to get into trouble.

40
00:04:54,424 --> 00:04:55,804
I understand.

41
00:04:57,368 --> 00:04:59,769
You found Paradise in America.

42
00:05:02,523 --> 00:05:07,091
You made a good living, had police
protection and there were courts of law.

43
00:05:07,417 --> 00:05:09,784
You didn't need a friend like me.

44
00:05:11,754 --> 00:05:15,333
But now you come to me and say,

45
00:05:15,358 --> 00:05:17,882
"Don Corleone, give me justice."

46
00:05:19,719 --> 00:05:22,547
But you don't ask with respect.

47
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:27,544
You don't offer friendship. You don't
even think to call me Godfather.

48
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:35,692
You come on my daughter's wedding
day and ask me to murder for money.

49
00:05:35,975 --> 00:05:38,466
I ask you for justice.

50
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:41,362
That is not justice.
Your daughter is alive.

51
00:05:42,703 --> 00:05:46,555
Let them suffer, then, as she suffers.

52
00:05:48,246 --> 00:05:50,969
How much shall I pay you?

53
00:06:05,238 --> 00:06:08,988
Bonasera, Bonasera.

54
00:06:09,263 --> 00:06:13,412
What have I ever done to make you
treat me so disrespectfully?

55
00:06:14,489 --> 00:06:17,061
If you'd come in friendship,

56
00:06:17,086 --> 00:06:21,506
the scum that ruined your daughter
would be suffering this very day.

57
00:06:22,666 --> 00:06:28,073
And if an honest man like you should
make enemies, they'd be my enemies.

58
00:06:30,842 --> 00:06:32,999
And then they would fear you.

59
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:39,189
Be my friend?

60
00:06:43,212 --> 00:06:45,365
Godfather?

61
00:06:49,103 --> 00:06:50,352
Good.

62
00:06:52,485 --> 00:06:57,708
Some day, and that day may never
come, I'll ask a service of you.

63
00:06:59,011 --> 00:07:01,881
But until that day...

64
00:07:02,824 --> 00:07:06,798
...accept this justice as a gift
on my daughter's wedding day.

65
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:09,922
- Grazie, Godfather.
- Prego.

66
00:07:16,237 --> 00:07:19,761
Give this to Clemenza.

67
00:07:21,771 --> 00:07:25,253
I want people that aren't going to
get carried away.

68
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:29,322
We're not murderers,
in spite of what this undertaker says.

69
00:07:54,778 --> 00:07:58,028
- Where's Michael?
- Don't worry, he'll be here.

70
00:07:59,189 --> 00:08:02,143
We're not taking the picture
without Michael.

71
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:11,525
- What's the matter?
- It's Michael.

72
00:09:00,849 --> 00:09:02,889
Don Barzini.

73
00:09:19,076 --> 00:09:22,243
Hey, Paulie! Let me have some wine.

74
00:09:22,268 --> 00:09:24,759
Paulie! More wine.

75
00:09:24,979 --> 00:09:29,688
- You look terrific on the floor.
- Are you a dance judge or something?

76
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:33,817
Take a walk around the
neighborhood, do your job.

77
00:09:41,637 --> 00:09:45,070
Sandra, watch the kids.
Don't let them run wild.

78
00:09:45,095 --> 00:09:47,447
You watch yourself, all right?

79
00:10:08,734 --> 00:10:12,862
20, 30 grand. In small bills, cash.

80
00:10:13,891 --> 00:10:15,967
In that little silk purse.

81
00:10:16,112 --> 00:10:19,695
If this were somebody else's wedding...
Sfortunato!

82
00:10:20,054 --> 00:10:21,382
Hey, Paulie!

83
00:10:25,313 --> 00:10:26,641
Stupid jerk!

84
00:10:35,298 --> 00:10:37,337
What's the matter?

85
00:10:49,604 --> 00:10:51,892
- Have to go back to work.
- Tom.

86
00:10:52,176 --> 00:10:53,090
Part of the wedding.

87
00:10:53,115 --> 00:10:56,116
No Sicilian can refuse any request
on his daughter's wedding day.

88
00:11:02,192 --> 00:11:07,302
Don Corleone, I'm honored and grateful
that you have invited me to your home.

89
00:11:12,116 --> 00:11:15,664
Get out of here!
It's a private party. Go on!

90
00:11:16,363 --> 00:11:18,828
What is it? It's my sister's wedding.

91
00:11:25,873 --> 00:11:28,486
Goddamn FBI don't respect nothing!

92
00:11:31,681 --> 00:11:34,552
Come here, come here, come here!

93
00:11:49,266 --> 00:11:53,975
...but towards the end, he was paroled
to help with the American war effort,

94
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,871
so for six months he's worked
in my pastry shop.

95
00:11:57,087 --> 00:11:59,245
Nazorine, what can I do for you?

96
00:11:59,658 --> 00:12:01,816
Now that the war is over,

97
00:12:01,841 --> 00:12:05,481
this boy, Enzo, they want to
repatriate him back to Italy.

98
00:12:06,138 --> 00:12:11,345
Godfather, I have a daughter.
You see, she and Enzo...

99
00:12:12,226 --> 00:12:17,176
You want Enzo to stay in this country,
and your daughter to be married.

100
00:12:17,887 --> 00:12:20,045
You understand everything.

101
00:12:20,985 --> 00:12:23,606
Mr Hagen. Thank you.

102
00:12:26,574 --> 00:12:29,536
Wait till you see the wedding cake
I made for your daughter!

103
00:12:30,738 --> 00:12:33,396
The bride, the groom and the angel...

104
00:12:38,604 --> 00:12:42,250
- Who should I give this job to?
- Not to our paisá.

105
00:12:43,217 --> 00:12:46,443
Give it to a Jew Congressman
in another district.

106
00:12:47,122 --> 00:12:48,697
Who else is on the list?

107
00:12:55,446 --> 00:12:57,652
Hey, Michael!

108
00:13:16,872 --> 00:13:19,712
He's not on the list,
but Luca Brasi wants to see you.

109
00:13:26,097 --> 00:13:28,646
Is this necessary?

110
00:13:28,671 --> 00:13:32,552
He didn't expect to be invited to the
wedding, so he wanted to thank you.

111
00:13:34,502 --> 00:13:40,105
Don Corleone, I'm honored and grateful
that you have invited me to your home

112
00:13:40,130 --> 00:13:45,646
on the wedding day of your daughter.
May their first child be a masculine child.

113
00:13:46,663 --> 00:13:48,216
Michael...

114
00:13:49,806 --> 00:13:52,083
That man over there
is talking to himself.

115
00:13:53,277 --> 00:13:55,446
See that scary guy over there?

116
00:13:56,472 --> 00:13:59,617
- He's a very scary guy.
- What's his name?

117
00:13:59,642 --> 00:14:04,553
His name is Luca Brasi.
He helps my father out sometimes.

118
00:14:06,283 --> 00:14:09,200
Michael, he's coming over here!

119
00:14:13,454 --> 00:14:15,333
You look terrific!

120
00:14:15,358 --> 00:14:18,692
My brother Tom Hagen,
Miss Kay Adams.

121
00:14:20,403 --> 00:14:22,338
Your father's been asking for you.

122
00:14:22,776 --> 00:14:25,776
- Very nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

123
00:14:27,421 --> 00:14:30,212
If he's your brother why does
he have a different name?

124
00:14:30,237 --> 00:14:34,112
My brother Sonny found
Tom Hagen in the street.

125
00:14:34,137 --> 00:14:38,383
He had no home,
so my father took him in.

126
00:14:39,876 --> 00:14:41,844
He's been with us ever since.

127
00:14:42,874 --> 00:14:44,257
He's a good lawyer.

128
00:14:45,627 --> 00:14:50,015
Not a Sicilian. I think he's
going to be consigliere.

129
00:14:50,475 --> 00:14:52,745
- What's that?
- That's a...

130
00:14:53,431 --> 00:14:57,892
...like a counselor, an advisor.
Very important for the family.

131
00:14:58,249 --> 00:15:00,036
You like your lasagna?

132
00:15:04,657 --> 00:15:06,240
Don Corleone.

133
00:15:07,023 --> 00:15:09,584
I'm honored and grateful

134
00:15:09,609 --> 00:15:13,328
that you have invited me
to your daughter's wedding.

135
00:15:18,589 --> 00:15:21,207
On the day of your daughter's wedding.

136
00:15:21,857 --> 00:15:27,026
And I hope that their first child
will be a masculine child.

137
00:15:28,228 --> 00:15:33,756
I pledge my ever-ending loyalty.

138
00:15:35,292 --> 00:15:40,216
- For your daughter's bridal purse.
- Thank you, Luca. Most valued friend.

139
00:15:40,784 --> 00:15:45,639
Don Corleone, I'm going to leave you
now, because I know you're busy.

140
00:15:46,383 --> 00:15:47,578
Thank you.

141
00:16:37,487 --> 00:16:39,610
Signora Corleone!

142
00:16:40,915 --> 00:16:42,742
No!

143
00:17:52,644 --> 00:17:57,520
Senator Cauley apologized for not
coming, but said you'd understand.

144
00:17:57,759 --> 00:18:02,136
Also some of the judges.
They've all sent gifts.

145
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:06,704
What is that outside?

146
00:18:15,542 --> 00:18:18,626
Johnny! Johnny!

147
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:22,920
I love you!

148
00:18:33,003 --> 00:18:36,537
He came all the way from California.
I told you he'd come!

149
00:18:36,562 --> 00:18:40,558
- He's probably in trouble again.
- He's a good godson.

150
00:18:41,148 --> 00:18:45,857
Johnny, Johnny! Sing a song!

151
00:19:01,106 --> 00:19:03,728
You never said you knew
Johnny Fontane!

152
00:19:03,988 --> 00:19:08,110
- Sure. You want to meet him?
- Great! Sure.

153
00:19:08,135 --> 00:19:12,002
- My father helped him with his career.
- He did?

154
00:19:12,222 --> 00:19:14,262
How?

155
00:19:15,298 --> 00:19:18,583
- Let's listen to this song.
- Michael...

156
00:19:51,796 --> 00:19:54,038
Please, Michael. Tell me.

157
00:19:57,600 --> 00:20:02,511
When Johnny was starting out, he was
signed to a personal service contract

158
00:20:02,536 --> 00:20:04,145
with a big bandleader.

159
00:20:05,677 --> 00:20:09,556
And as his career got better and better,
he wanted to get out of it.

160
00:20:10,991 --> 00:20:13,032
Johnny is my father's godson.

161
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:16,722
My father went to see this bandleader.

162
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:20,868
He offered him 10,000 dollars
to let Johnny go,

163
00:20:20,893 --> 00:20:22,598
but the bandleader said no.

164
00:20:23,793 --> 00:20:29,333
So the next day my father went to see
him, but this time with Luca Brasi.

165
00:20:31,092 --> 00:20:33,168
Within an hour,

166
00:20:33,193 --> 00:20:38,987
he signed a release
for a certified check of 1,000 dollars.

167
00:20:40,752 --> 00:20:44,880
- How did he do that?
- Made him an offer he couldn't refuse.

168
00:20:46,419 --> 00:20:51,211
- What was that?
- Luca Brasi held a gun to his head,

169
00:20:51,236 --> 00:20:56,479
and father said that either his brains or
his signature would be on the contract.

170
00:21:01,538 --> 00:21:03,447
That's a true story.

171
00:21:14,891 --> 00:21:17,216
That's my family, Kay. It's not me.

172
00:21:29,887 --> 00:21:31,926
Beautiful!

173
00:22:03,872 --> 00:22:05,912
I'll take care of it.

174
00:22:06,267 --> 00:22:07,810
Tom...

175
00:22:08,301 --> 00:22:12,429
I want you to find Santino.
Tell him to come to the office.

176
00:22:19,103 --> 00:22:20,650
How are you, Fredo?

177
00:22:21,178 --> 00:22:24,677
My brother Fredo,
this is Kay Adams.

178
00:22:25,854 --> 00:22:28,345
- Hi.
- How are you doing?

179
00:22:30,103 --> 00:22:33,036
- This is my brother Mike.
- Are you having a good time?

180
00:22:33,061 --> 00:22:36,145
Yeah. This is your friend?

181
00:22:37,216 --> 00:22:42,506
I don't know what to do.
My voice is weak. It's weak.

182
00:22:43,711 --> 00:22:49,529
Anyway, if I had this part in the picture,
it puts me right back on top again.

183
00:22:50,283 --> 00:22:55,885
But this... man won't give it to me,
the head of the studio.

184
00:22:55,910 --> 00:22:58,336
- What's his name?
- Woltz.

185
00:22:59,111 --> 00:23:02,216
He won't give it to me,
and he says there's no chance.

186
00:23:02,254 --> 00:23:03,261
No chance.

187
00:23:07,326 --> 00:23:08,787
Sonny?

188
00:23:10,395 --> 00:23:11,616
Sonny?

189
00:23:17,949 --> 00:23:19,409
Sonny?

190
00:23:20,162 --> 00:23:22,632
- Sonny, are you in there?
- What?

191
00:23:22,802 --> 00:23:24,261
The old man wants you.

192
00:23:26,074 --> 00:23:27,641
One minute.

193
00:23:41,973 --> 00:23:46,967
A month ago he bought the movie rights
to this book, a best-seller.

194
00:23:46,992 --> 00:23:50,325
The main character
is a guy just like me.

195
00:23:50,672 --> 00:23:53,507
I wouldn't even have to act.

196
00:23:54,614 --> 00:23:57,372
Godfather, I don't know what to do.

197
00:23:58,732 --> 00:24:02,356
You can act like a man!
What's the matter with you?

198
00:24:03,173 --> 00:24:07,402
Is this how you turned out a Hollywood
finocchio, that cries like a woman?

199
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:11,573
"What can I do?
What can I do?"

200
00:24:11,598 --> 00:24:14,084
What is that nonsense?
Ridiculous.

201
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:22,274
- You spend time with your family?
- Sure I do.

202
00:24:22,741 --> 00:24:23,980
Good.

203
00:24:24,328 --> 00:24:28,407
Because a man who doesn't spend time
with his family can never be a real man.

204
00:24:34,595 --> 00:24:37,521
You look terrible. I want you to eat.

205
00:24:38,095 --> 00:24:43,166
Rest, and in a month this Hollywood
big shot will give you what you want.

206
00:24:43,570 --> 00:24:46,465
It's too late, they start shooting
in a week.

207
00:24:46,891 --> 00:24:49,457
I'm going to make him an offer
he can't refuse.

208
00:24:52,716 --> 00:24:58,302
Just go outside and enjoy yourself,
and forget about all this nonsense.

209
00:25:00,137 --> 00:25:03,222
- I want you to leave it all to me.
- All right.

210
00:25:28,218 --> 00:25:33,085
- What time does my daughter leave?
- Soon, after they cut the cake.

211
00:25:33,485 --> 00:25:37,336
Do we give your son-in-law
something important?

212
00:25:37,361 --> 00:25:42,350
Never. Give him a living, but never
discuss the family business with him.

213
00:25:42,644 --> 00:25:45,182
- What else?
- Virgil Sollozzo called.

214
00:25:45,572 --> 00:25:49,896
- We'll have to see him next week.
- When you come back from California.

215
00:25:51,316 --> 00:25:54,698
- When am I going to California?
- I want you to go tonight.

216
00:25:54,723 --> 00:25:59,954
I want you to talk to this movie big shot
and settle this business for Johnny.

217
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:04,515
If there's nothing else, I'd like to go
to my daughter's wedding.

218
00:26:07,489 --> 00:26:10,340
Carlo, we're going to take the picture.

219
00:26:11,482 --> 00:26:13,356
Wait a minute.

220
00:26:13,381 --> 00:26:15,324
No, Michael. Not me.

221
00:26:18,835 --> 00:26:22,833
Okay, that's it. Just like that. Hold it!

222
00:28:13,234 --> 00:28:16,973
- You need a little more heat on that arc.
- Start talking.

223
00:28:16,998 --> 00:28:19,750
I was sent by a friend
of Johnny Fontane.

224
00:28:20,125 --> 00:28:23,889
This friend would give
his friendship to Mr Woltz,

225
00:28:23,914 --> 00:28:26,850
if Mr Woltz would grant us a favour.

226
00:28:26,875 --> 00:28:28,445
Woltz is listening.

227
00:28:29,225 --> 00:28:32,598
Give Johnny the part in that new
war film you're starting next week.

228
00:28:38,995 --> 00:28:44,030
And what favour would your friend
grant Mr Woltz?

229
00:28:44,055 --> 00:28:47,438
He could make your future union
problems disappear.

230
00:28:47,638 --> 00:28:51,509
And one of your stars has just moved
from marijuana to heroin.

231
00:28:51,534 --> 00:28:56,292
Are you trying to muscle me?
Listen, you son-of-a-bitch!

232
00:28:56,317 --> 00:29:01,114
Let me lay it on the line. Johnny
Fontane will never get that movie!

233
00:29:01,139 --> 00:29:05,579
No matter how many Dago Guinea
greaseballs come out of the woodwork!

234
00:29:05,604 --> 00:29:09,479
- I'm German-Irish.
- Listen here, my Kraut-Mick friend.

235
00:29:09,504 --> 00:29:14,141
- I'm going to make trouble for you!
- I'm a lawyer. I have not threatened...

236
00:29:14,166 --> 00:29:16,232
I know almost every
big lawyer in New York.

237
00:29:16,257 --> 00:29:17,565
Who the hell are you?

238
00:29:17,590 --> 00:29:20,124
I have a special practice.
I handle one client.

239
00:29:21,130 --> 00:29:23,017
Now you have my number,
I'll wait for your call.

240
00:29:24,927 --> 00:29:27,702
By the way, I admire your pictures
very much.

241
00:29:32,597 --> 00:29:34,124
Check him out.

242
00:29:56,516 --> 00:29:59,185
- It's really beautiful.
- Look at this.

243
00:29:59,210 --> 00:30:01,480
It used to decorate
the palace of a king.

244
00:30:01,504 --> 00:30:02,434
Very nice.

245
00:30:03,879 --> 00:30:06,477
Why didn't you say
you work for Corleone?

246
00:30:06,502 --> 00:30:10,582
I thought you were some cheap hustler
Johnny was running in.

247
00:30:10,761 --> 00:30:14,126
- I only use his name when necessary.
- How's your drink?

248
00:30:14,224 --> 00:30:17,238
- Fine.
- Now I'll show you something beautiful.

249
00:30:17,753 --> 00:30:19,832
You do appreciate beauty, don't you?

250
00:30:22,951 --> 00:30:26,584
There you are.
$600,000 on four hooves.

251
00:30:26,609 --> 00:30:30,160
I'll bet Russian czars never
paid that for a single horse.

252
00:30:30,420 --> 00:30:32,256
Khartoum.

253
00:30:32,634 --> 00:30:34,020
Khartoum.

254
00:30:35,317 --> 00:30:40,090
I'm not going to race him, though.
I'm going to put him out to stud.

255
00:30:41,292 --> 00:30:42,834
Thanks, Tony.

256
00:30:43,046 --> 00:30:46,213
Let's get something to eat.

257
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:49,883
Corleone is Johnny's godfather.

258
00:30:50,438 --> 00:30:54,202
To the Italian people that's
a very sacred, close relationship.

259
00:30:54,603 --> 00:31:00,596
I respect it. Tell him to ask me anything
else. This favour I can't give him.

260
00:31:01,146 --> 00:31:04,061
He never asks a second favour
when he's been refused the first.

261
00:31:04,636 --> 00:31:09,549
You don't understand. Johnny Fontane
never gets that movie.

262
00:31:10,715 --> 00:31:14,201
That part is perfect for him.
It'll make him a big star.

263
00:31:14,608 --> 00:31:18,449
I'm going to run him out of the business,
and let me tell you why.

264
00:31:20,621 --> 00:31:25,045
Johnny Fontane ruined one of Woltz
International's most valuable protégés.

265
00:31:25,513 --> 00:31:30,933
We trained her for five years.
Singing, acting, dancing lessons.

266
00:31:30,958 --> 00:31:35,611
I spent hundreds of thousands of dollars
on her, I was gonna make her a big star.

267
00:31:35,636 --> 00:31:38,032
Let me be even more frank.

268
00:31:38,416 --> 00:31:43,123
To show you that I'm not a hard-hearted
man. That it's not all dollars and cents.

269
00:31:43,581 --> 00:31:46,870
She was beautiful.
She was young and innocent!

270
00:31:47,263 --> 00:31:51,766
She's the greatest piece of ass I've had
and I've had them all over the world.

271
00:31:52,734 --> 00:31:58,373
Then Johnny Fontane comes along with
his olive oil voice and Guinea charm.

272
00:31:59,005 --> 00:32:00,813
And she runs off.

273
00:32:01,993 --> 00:32:05,571
She threw it all away
just to make me look ridiculous!

274
00:32:06,171 --> 00:32:10,980
And a man in my position can't afford
to be made to look ridiculous!

275
00:32:11,494 --> 00:32:13,757
Now you get the hell out of here!

276
00:32:13,782 --> 00:32:18,195
If that goombah tries any rough stuff,
tell him I'm no bandleader.

277
00:32:19,522 --> 00:32:22,635
Yeah, I heard that story.

278
00:32:23,432 --> 00:32:26,950
Thank you for dinner
and a very pleasant evening.

279
00:32:27,335 --> 00:32:29,496
Maybe your car can take me
to the airport.

280
00:32:30,384 --> 00:32:33,803
Mr Corleone insists on hearing
bad news immediately.

281
00:34:26,629 --> 00:34:30,162
- You're not too tired, are you, Tom?
- No, I slept on the plane.

282
00:34:30,541 --> 00:34:33,459
I have the Sollozzo notes here.

283
00:34:33,670 --> 00:34:35,828
Now...

284
00:34:37,004 --> 00:34:42,737
Sollozzo is known as The Turk. He's
supposed to be very good with a knife,

285
00:34:42,762 --> 00:34:46,739
but only in matters of business
with reasonable complaint.

286
00:34:47,246 --> 00:34:49,760
His business is narcotics.

287
00:34:50,586 --> 00:34:53,299
He has fields in Turkey,
where they grow poppy.

288
00:34:53,753 --> 00:34:57,645
In Sicily he has plants to process them
into heroin.

289
00:34:57,860 --> 00:35:01,737
He needs cash, he needs protection
from the police.

290
00:35:01,762 --> 00:35:05,427
He'll give a piece of the action.
I don't know how much.

291
00:35:05,728 --> 00:35:10,348
The Tattaglia family is behind him here.
They have to be in it for something.

292
00:35:12,143 --> 00:35:16,217
- What about his prison record?
- One term in Italy, one here.

293
00:35:16,910 --> 00:35:19,071
He's known as a top narcotics man.

294
00:35:19,776 --> 00:35:24,668
- Santino, what do you think?
- A lot of money in that white powder.

295
00:35:26,704 --> 00:35:27,818
Tom?

296
00:35:28,098 --> 00:35:32,421
Yes. There's more money in narcotics
than anything else.

297
00:35:32,446 --> 00:35:37,278
If we don't get into it, somebody else
will, maybe the five families.

298
00:35:37,303 --> 00:35:41,436
With that money they can buy
more police and political power.

299
00:35:41,841 --> 00:35:43,880
Then they come after us.

300
00:35:43,905 --> 00:35:50,478
Now we have unions and gambling, and
that's great, but narcotics is the future.

301
00:35:50,503 --> 00:35:55,867
If we don't get a piece of that action,
we risk everything in ten years' time.

302
00:35:59,921 --> 00:36:03,207
So? What's your answer
going to be, Pop?

303
00:36:08,109 --> 00:36:10,214
Don Corleone.

304
00:36:11,981 --> 00:36:14,669
I need a man who has powerful friends.

305
00:36:15,433 --> 00:36:17,386
I need a million dollars in cash.

306
00:36:18,113 --> 00:36:24,182
I need those politicians that you carry
in your pocket, like nickels and dimes.

307
00:36:25,484 --> 00:36:29,112
- What is the interest for my family?
- 30 per cent.

308
00:36:29,551 --> 00:36:33,102
In the first year your end should be
three, four million dollars.

309
00:36:33,751 --> 00:36:35,450
And then it would go up.

310
00:36:36,763 --> 00:36:39,882
And what is the interest
for the Tattaglia family?

311
00:36:42,295 --> 00:36:43,850
My compliments.

312
00:36:47,617 --> 00:36:50,404
I'll take care of them, out of my share.

313
00:36:51,112 --> 00:36:55,394
So I receive 30 per cent for finance,

314
00:36:55,419 --> 00:36:58,705
political influence and legal protection?

315
00:36:58,981 --> 00:37:00,816
That's right.

316
00:37:01,915 --> 00:37:05,919
Why do you come to me?
Why do I deserve this generosity?

317
00:37:05,944 --> 00:37:11,112
If you consider a million
dollars in cash just finance,

318
00:37:11,137 --> 00:37:13,924
ti saluto, Don Corleone.

319
00:37:23,824 --> 00:37:29,067
I said that I would see you, because
I heard you were a serious man,

320
00:37:29,092 --> 00:37:31,381
to be treated with respect.

321
00:37:36,309 --> 00:37:39,844
But, I must say no to you.

322
00:37:40,686 --> 00:37:43,364
And I'll give you my reason.

323
00:37:43,675 --> 00:37:46,429
It's true, I have a lot of friends in politics.

324
00:37:47,741 --> 00:37:52,316
They wouldn't be friendly long if I was
involved in drugs instead of gambling,

325
00:37:52,341 --> 00:37:57,797
which they regard as a harmless vice,
but drugs is a dirty business.

326
00:37:58,120 --> 00:38:02,116
It doesn't make any difference to me
what a man does for a living.

327
00:38:03,059 --> 00:38:08,160
But your business is...
a little dangerous.

328
00:38:08,512 --> 00:38:12,863
If you're worried about security,
the Tattaglias will guarantee it.

329
00:38:12,888 --> 00:38:16,719
- The Tattaglias would guarantee our...
- Wait a minute.

330
00:38:23,740 --> 00:38:28,250
I have a sentimental weakness
for my children, and I spoil them.

331
00:38:28,275 --> 00:38:31,976
They talk when they should listen.
But anyway...

332
00:38:32,169 --> 00:38:38,073
Signor Sollozzo, my no is final. I wish to
congratulate you on your new business.

333
00:38:38,098 --> 00:38:40,829
I know you'll do well, and good luck.

334
00:38:40,854 --> 00:38:46,014
Especially since your interests
don't conflict with mine. Thank you.

335
00:39:06,644 --> 00:39:08,373
Santino.

336
00:39:08,398 --> 00:39:09,809
Come here.

337
00:39:12,277 --> 00:39:19,026
What's the matter with you? Your brain
is going soft from playing with that girl.

338
00:39:19,408 --> 00:39:23,472
Never tell anybody outside the family
what you're thinking again.

339
00:39:24,730 --> 00:39:25,959
Go on.

340
00:39:29,938 --> 00:39:33,080
Tom, what's this nonsense?

341
00:39:33,105 --> 00:39:36,108
It's from Johnny.
He's starring in that new film.

342
00:39:38,651 --> 00:39:41,735
- Take it away.
- Take it over there.

343
00:39:42,513 --> 00:39:44,137
And...

344
00:39:45,073 --> 00:39:47,491
...tell Luca Brasi to come in.

345
00:39:53,380 --> 00:39:56,795
I'm a little worried
about this Sollozzo fellow.

346
00:39:56,820 --> 00:39:59,849
Find out what he's got
under his fingernails.

347
00:40:00,925 --> 00:40:03,595
Go to the Tattaglias.

348
00:40:04,554 --> 00:40:09,787
Make them think that you're not
too happy with our family

349
00:40:09,812 --> 00:40:12,897
and find out what you can.

350
00:40:29,811 --> 00:40:33,482
I got something for your
mother and for Sonny

351
00:40:33,508 --> 00:40:37,960
and a tie for Freddy, and
Tom Hagen got the Reynolds pen.

352
00:40:38,393 --> 00:40:42,521
- What do you want for Christmas?
- Just you.

353
00:41:13,249 --> 00:41:15,206
Andiamo, Fredo.

354
00:41:15,231 --> 00:41:18,647
- Tell Paulie to get the car.
- Okay, Pop.

355
00:41:18,859 --> 00:41:22,987
I'll have to get it myself.
Paulie called in sick this morning.

356
00:41:24,606 --> 00:41:27,332
Paulie's a good kid.
I don't mind getting the car.

357
00:41:31,269 --> 00:41:33,345
Buon Natale, caro. Grazie.

358
00:42:16,115 --> 00:42:20,492
- Luca! I'm Bruno Tattaglia.
- I know.

359
00:42:30,437 --> 00:42:31,765
You know who I am?

360
00:44:10,403 --> 00:44:13,606
Tom! Tom Hagen. Merry Christmas.

361
00:44:14,334 --> 00:44:18,996
- Glad to see you. I want to talk to you.
- I haven't got time.

362
00:44:19,162 --> 00:44:23,029
Make time, Consigliere. Get in the car.

363
00:44:24,007 --> 00:44:28,669
What are you worried about? If I wanted
to kill you, you'd be dead already.

364
00:44:28,914 --> 00:44:30,539
Get in.

365
00:44:41,416 --> 00:44:45,366
- Fredo, I'm going to buy some fruit.
- Okay, Pop.

366
00:44:51,360 --> 00:44:54,693
Merry Christmas. I want some fruit.

367
00:46:21,865 --> 00:46:26,362
Would you like me better
if I were a nun? Like in the story.

368
00:46:29,270 --> 00:46:30,451
No.

369
00:46:30,666 --> 00:46:35,162
- What if I were Ingrid Bergman?
- Now, that's a thought.

370
00:46:37,130 --> 00:46:38,922
Michael.

371
00:46:39,132 --> 00:46:44,257
No, I wouldn't like you better if you were
Ingrid Bergman. What's the matter?

372
00:47:00,730 --> 00:47:03,351
They don't say if he's dead or alive.

373
00:47:25,236 --> 00:47:28,486
- Sonny, it's Michael.
- Where have you been?

374
00:47:28,954 --> 00:47:31,576
- Is he all right?
- We don't know yet.

375
00:47:32,013 --> 00:47:36,322
There are all kinds of stories.
He was hit bad, Mikey.

376
00:47:37,668 --> 00:47:40,530
- Are you there?
- Yeah, I'm here.

377
00:47:41,336 --> 00:47:45,423
- Where have you been? I was worried.
- Didn't Tom tell you I called?

378
00:47:45,573 --> 00:47:50,282
No. Look, come home, kid.
You should be with Mama, you hear?

379
00:47:57,376 --> 00:47:59,582
Oh, my God.

380
00:48:03,327 --> 00:48:04,569
Sonny!

381
00:48:13,521 --> 00:48:15,661
Stay back there.

382
00:48:15,686 --> 00:48:18,852
- Who is it?
- Open up, it's Clemenza.

383
00:48:20,698 --> 00:48:23,818
There's more news about your old man.

384
00:48:24,229 --> 00:48:26,934
Word is out that he's already dead.

385
00:48:27,182 --> 00:48:30,801
- What's the matter with you?
- Take it easy!

386
00:48:30,826 --> 00:48:34,029
- Where was Paulie?
- Sick. He's been sick all winter.

387
00:48:34,246 --> 00:48:36,973
- How often?
- Only three, four times.

388
00:48:36,998 --> 00:48:40,699
- Freddy didn't want a new bodyguard.
- Pick him up now.

389
00:48:40,919 --> 00:48:45,331
I don't care how sick he is. Bring him
to my father's house right now.

390
00:48:45,675 --> 00:48:49,281
- You want anyone sent over here?
- No. Go ahead.

391
00:48:56,258 --> 00:49:00,251
I'm going to have a couple of our people
come over to the house.

392
00:49:04,484 --> 00:49:06,772
- Hello?
- Santino Corleone?

393
00:49:06,986 --> 00:49:09,821
- Yeah.
- We have Tom Hagen.

394
00:49:09,846 --> 00:49:13,215
In three hours he'll be released
with our proposition.

395
00:49:13,717 --> 00:49:16,967
Listen to what he has to say
before you do anything.

396
00:49:17,179 --> 00:49:21,757
What's done is done. Don't lose that
famous temper of yours, Sonny.

397
00:49:21,948 --> 00:49:23,448
I'll wait.

398
00:49:37,857 --> 00:49:39,924
Your boss is dead.

399
00:49:42,704 --> 00:49:47,262
I know you're not in the muscle end
of the family, so don't be scared.

400
00:49:48,217 --> 00:49:52,732
I want you to help the Corleones
and me.

401
00:49:56,169 --> 00:50:00,041
We got him outside his office
about an hour after we picked you up.

402
00:50:02,258 --> 00:50:03,457
Drink it.

403
00:50:08,116 --> 00:50:11,243
It's up to you to make peace
between me and Sonny.

404
00:50:15,844 --> 00:50:18,590
Sonny was hot for my deal, wasn't he?

405
00:50:19,916 --> 00:50:22,310
And you knew
it was the right thing to do.

406
00:50:23,936 --> 00:50:29,462
- Sonny will come after you.
- That will be his first reaction, sure.

407
00:50:30,587 --> 00:50:36,372
So you have to talk sense into him.
The Tattaglia family is behind me.

408
00:50:37,132 --> 00:50:41,822
The other New York families will go
along with anything to prevent war.

409
00:50:42,319 --> 00:50:47,906
Let's face it, with all due respect,
the Don - rest in peace - was slipping.

410
00:50:50,601 --> 00:50:52,963
Ten years ago,
could I have gotten to him?

411
00:50:57,330 --> 00:51:01,552
Well, now he's dead, Tom,
and nothing can bring him back.

412
00:51:03,084 --> 00:51:09,502
You've got to talk to Sonny, to the
Caporegimes, Tessio, fat Clemenza.

413
00:51:13,694 --> 00:51:16,349
It's good business, Tom.

414
00:51:17,396 --> 00:51:22,530
I'll try. But even Sonny won't be able
to call off Luca Brasi.

415
00:51:25,403 --> 00:51:27,609
Yeah, well...

416
00:51:28,908 --> 00:51:31,577
Let me worry about Luca.

417
00:51:36,665 --> 00:51:38,458
You just talk to Sonny.

418
00:51:39,053 --> 00:51:40,965
And the other two kids.

419
00:51:44,295 --> 00:51:47,318
- I'll do my best.
- Good.

420
00:51:49,141 --> 00:51:52,010
Now you can go.

421
00:51:58,424 --> 00:52:02,292
I don't like violence, Tom.
I'm a businessman.

422
00:52:03,153 --> 00:52:06,237
Blood is a big expense.

423
00:52:26,978 --> 00:52:28,743
He's still alive.

424
00:52:28,768 --> 00:52:31,782
They hit him with five shots,
and he's still alive!

425
00:52:33,076 --> 00:52:37,681
That's bad luck for me, and bad luck
for you if you don't make that deal.

426
00:53:22,056 --> 00:53:26,369
Your mother is at the hospital with
your father. Looks like he'll pull through.

427
00:53:28,816 --> 00:53:35,433
It's a lot of bad blood. Sollozzo, Philip
Tattaglia, Bruno Tattaglia, Ramon...

428
00:53:35,458 --> 00:53:38,329
- You gonna kill all those guys?
- Stay out of it.

429
00:53:38,545 --> 00:53:41,499
If you get rid of Sollozzo,
everything falls into line.

430
00:53:41,714 --> 00:53:45,000
What about Luca?
Sollozzo thinks he can control him.

431
00:53:45,953 --> 00:53:49,822
If Luca sold out, we're in a lot of trouble.

432
00:53:49,847 --> 00:53:53,785
- Has anyone been in touch with Luca?
- We've been trying all night.

433
00:53:53,810 --> 00:53:58,555
- Hey, do me a favour...
- Luca never sleeps over with a broad.

434
00:53:59,753 --> 00:54:05,678
Well, Tom, you're consigliere.
What do we do if the old man dies?

435
00:54:06,051 --> 00:54:12,149
If we lose the old man, we lose the
political contacts and half our strength.

436
00:54:12,411 --> 00:54:18,139
The other New York families might
support Sollozzo to avoid a long war.

437
00:54:18,164 --> 00:54:21,994
This is almost 1946.
Nobody wants bloodshed anymore.

438
00:54:22,760 --> 00:54:24,468
If your father dies...

439
00:54:26,841 --> 00:54:28,444
...you make the deal.

440
00:54:28,797 --> 00:54:33,577
- Easy to say. He's not your father.
- I'm as much a son as you or Mike.

441
00:54:38,121 --> 00:54:40,289
What is it?

442
00:54:40,314 --> 00:54:46,091
- Paulie, I told you to stay put.
- The guy at the gates has a package.

443
00:54:46,214 --> 00:54:49,499
Tessio, go see what it is.

444
00:54:51,946 --> 00:54:54,401
- Want me to hang around?
- Yeah, hang around. Are you all right?

445
00:54:54,426 --> 00:54:57,973
- Yeah, I'm fine.
- There's food. Are you hungry?

446
00:54:57,998 --> 00:55:01,449
- No.
- A drink? Brandy will sweat it out.

447
00:55:01,940 --> 00:55:04,610
- Go ahead.
- That might be a good idea.

448
00:55:06,275 --> 00:55:11,211
Take care of that son-of-a-bitch.
Paulie sold out the old man.

449
00:55:11,236 --> 00:55:15,507
- Make that the first thing on your list.
- Understood.

450
00:55:16,053 --> 00:55:19,836
Mickey, tomorrow, get some guys
and go to Luca's apartment.

451
00:55:20,416 --> 00:55:24,366
Maybe we shouldn't get Mike
mixed up in this too directly.

452
00:55:26,662 --> 00:55:30,059
Hanging around the house on
the phone would be a big help.

453
00:55:31,204 --> 00:55:33,493
Try Luca again.

454
00:55:41,866 --> 00:55:44,900
- What's this?
- A Sicilian message.

455
00:55:44,925 --> 00:55:48,055
It means Luca Brasi
sleeps with the fishes.

456
00:56:01,546 --> 00:56:03,787
- I'm going.
- When will you be home?

457
00:56:03,812 --> 00:56:05,538
I don't know, probably late.

458
00:56:07,905 --> 00:56:11,654
- Don't forget the cannoli!
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

459
00:56:13,808 --> 00:56:18,435
Rocco, sit on the other side.
You block the rear-view mirror.

460
00:56:19,600 --> 00:56:23,636
Sonny's running wild. He wants
to go to mattresses already.

461
00:56:23,661 --> 00:56:28,962
We have to find a spot on the
West Side. Try 309 West 43rd Street.

462
00:56:29,407 --> 00:56:33,089
- Know a good spot on the West Side?
- I'll think about it.

463
00:56:33,114 --> 00:56:36,466
Think while you're driving.
I want to hit New York this month.

464
00:56:36,913 --> 00:56:38,822
Watch out for the kids
when you're backing out.

465
00:56:49,570 --> 00:56:55,426
Paulie, go down 39th Street, pick up
18 mattresses and bring me the bill.

466
00:56:55,451 --> 00:56:56,589
Yeah, all right.

467
00:56:56,914 --> 00:57:01,327
Make sure they're clean, because
the guys will be there a long time.

468
00:57:01,728 --> 00:57:05,856
- They're clean and exterminated.
- That's a bad word to use.

469
00:57:05,881 --> 00:57:09,749
Exterminate! Watch out,
so we don't exterminate you!

470
00:57:16,442 --> 00:57:18,475
Pull over. I've got to take a leak.

471
00:58:00,855 --> 00:58:04,105
Leave the gun. Take the cannoli.

472
00:58:22,307 --> 00:58:25,392
Hey, Mike! Hey, Mikey!

473
00:58:27,072 --> 00:58:29,029
- Yeah.
- Phone call!

474
00:58:35,229 --> 00:58:37,684
- Who is it?
- Some girl.

475
00:58:41,667 --> 00:58:43,955
- Hello. Kay?
- How's your father?

476
00:58:44,224 --> 00:58:45,967
He's going to make it.

477
00:58:46,897 --> 00:58:48,937
I love you.

478
00:58:49,707 --> 00:58:51,747
I love you!

479
00:58:52,507 --> 00:58:54,998
- Michael?
- Yeah, I know.

480
00:58:55,411 --> 00:58:58,198
- Tell me you love me.
- I can't talk.

481
00:58:58,274 --> 00:59:00,516
Can't you say it?

482
00:59:01,152 --> 00:59:02,979
I'll see you tonight.

483
00:59:03,814 --> 00:59:06,898
Hey Mikey! Why didn't you tell
that nice girl you love her?

484
00:59:07,017 --> 00:59:11,893
I love you with all my heart. If I don't
see you again soon, I'm going to die!

485
00:59:12,936 --> 00:59:17,420
Come and learn something. You might
have to cook for 20 guys some day.

486
00:59:18,480 --> 00:59:21,707
You start with a little oil,
then fry some garlic.

487
00:59:21,732 --> 00:59:26,800
Throw in some tomatoes, tomato paste,
fry it and make sure it doesn't stick.

488
00:59:27,226 --> 00:59:31,051
You get it to a boil, you shove in
all your sausage and meatballs.

489
00:59:33,220 --> 00:59:35,671
Add a little bit of wine.

490
00:59:38,563 --> 00:59:43,344
And a little bit of sugar. That's my trick.

491
00:59:43,369 --> 00:59:47,501
Cut the crap. I have more important
things for you. How's Paulie?

492
00:59:47,538 --> 00:59:50,574
You won't see him anymore.

493
00:59:51,085 --> 00:59:53,837
- Where are you going?
- To the city.

494
00:59:53,862 --> 00:59:57,435
- Send bodyguards with him.
- I'm going to the hospital...

495
00:59:57,460 --> 01:00:00,253
He'll be all right. Sollozzo knows
he's a civilian.

496
01:00:01,012 --> 01:00:03,717
- Be careful, huh?
- Yes, sir.

497
01:00:06,058 --> 01:00:08,265
Send somebody with him anyway.

498
01:00:36,583 --> 01:00:39,750
- I have to go.
- Can I go with you?

499
01:00:41,109 --> 01:00:45,570
No, Kay. There will be detectives there,
people from the press.

500
01:00:45,848 --> 01:00:48,303
I'll wait in the cab.

501
01:00:50,283 --> 01:00:52,777
I don't want you to get involved.

502
01:00:55,663 --> 01:00:58,095
When will I see you again?

503
01:01:04,241 --> 01:01:08,534
Go back to New Hampshire, and I'll
call you at your parents' house.

504
01:01:10,080 --> 01:01:15,157
- When will I see you again, Michael?
- I don't know.

505
01:03:27,023 --> 01:03:30,919
What are you doing here?
You're not supposed to be here.

506
01:03:30,944 --> 01:03:34,029
I'm Michael Corleone. This is my father.

507
01:03:34,579 --> 01:03:37,366
There's nobody here.
What happened to the guards?

508
01:03:37,391 --> 01:03:41,626
Your father had too many visitors.
They interfered with hospital service.

509
01:03:42,697 --> 01:03:45,611
The police made them leave
about ten minutes ago.

510
01:03:50,237 --> 01:03:54,400
Get me Long Beach 45620, please.

511
01:03:56,882 --> 01:03:59,966
Nurse. Wait a minute. Stay here.

512
01:04:03,250 --> 01:04:07,866
Sonny, I'm at the hospital.
I got here late, there's nobody here.

513
01:04:08,167 --> 01:04:12,264
No Tessio's men, no detectives,
nobody. Papa's all alone.

514
01:04:12,467 --> 01:04:15,219
- Don't panic.
- I won't panic.

515
01:04:16,431 --> 01:04:19,550
I'm sorry, but you will have to leave.

516
01:04:22,143 --> 01:04:27,849
We're going to move him to another
room. Can you disconnect the tubes?

517
01:04:28,066 --> 01:04:31,565
- That's out of the question!
- Do you know my father?

518
01:04:31,717 --> 01:04:35,349
Men are coming here to kill him.
Do you understand?

519
01:04:36,115 --> 01:04:38,238
Help me, please.

520
01:05:54,943 --> 01:05:58,941
- Who are you?
- I am Enzo, the baker.

521
01:05:59,781 --> 01:06:01,904
- Remember me?
- Enzo.

522
01:06:01,929 --> 01:06:04,799
You'd better go,
there's going to be trouble.

523
01:06:05,169 --> 01:06:09,961
If there is trouble, I'll stay here to
help you. For your father.

524
01:06:11,701 --> 01:06:15,876
Listen. Wait for me outside,
in front of the hospital, all right?

525
01:06:15,901 --> 01:06:18,024
I'll be out in a minute.

526
01:06:31,983 --> 01:06:36,069
Just lie here, Pop.
I'll take care of you now.

527
01:06:37,568 --> 01:06:39,810
I'm with you now.

528
01:06:41,197 --> 01:06:42,905
I'm with you.

529
01:07:18,233 --> 01:07:20,558
Get rid of these. Come here.

530
01:07:21,361 --> 01:07:25,769
Put your hand in your pocket, like you
have a gun. You'll be all right.

531
01:08:17,084 --> 01:08:19,290
You did good.

532
01:09:07,299 --> 01:09:09,460
I thought I got all you
Guinea hoods locked up!

533
01:09:09,485 --> 01:09:10,691
What the hell are
you doing here?

534
01:09:10,756 --> 01:09:14,968
- Why isn't anyone guarding my father?
- Why, you little punk!

535
01:09:15,371 --> 01:09:19,415
Don't you tell me my business!
I pulled them off.

536
01:09:19,479 --> 01:09:25,434
- Stay away from this hospital!
- Not until my father's room is guarded.

537
01:09:26,109 --> 01:09:29,193
- Phil, take him in!
- The kid's clean, Captain.

538
01:09:29,477 --> 01:09:33,186
- He's a war hero. He's never been...
- I said take him in!

539
01:09:35,413 --> 01:09:41,641
- What's The Turk paying you?
- Take a hold of him. Stand him up.

540
01:09:41,666 --> 01:09:43,623
Stand him up straight.

541
01:10:05,920 --> 01:10:11,187
I'm the Corleone's attorney. These men
are hired to protect Vito Corleone.

542
01:10:11,212 --> 01:10:13,652
They're licensed to carry firearms.

543
01:10:13,677 --> 01:10:18,470
If you interfere, you'll have to appear
before the judge and show cause.

544
01:10:18,495 --> 01:10:20,653
Let him go.

545
01:10:52,987 --> 01:10:56,735
- What's with all the new faces?
- We'll need them now.

546
01:10:56,956 --> 01:10:59,625
After the hospital thing, Sonny got mad.

547
01:10:59,967 --> 01:11:02,907
We hit Bruno Tattaglia this morning.

548
01:11:04,165 --> 01:11:05,695
Jesus Christ.

549
01:11:12,797 --> 01:11:15,881
Looks like a fortress around here.

550
01:11:17,552 --> 01:11:22,677
Tommasuccio! Hey... 100 buttonmen
on the street 24 hours a day.

551
01:11:22,932 --> 01:11:26,269
That Turk shows one hair on his ass,
he's dead.

552
01:11:28,688 --> 01:11:30,810
Mike, let me look at you.

553
01:11:34,693 --> 01:11:37,860
You're beautiful, beautiful.
You're gorgeous.

554
01:11:37,925 --> 01:11:43,345
The Turk wants to talk! Imagine
the nerve of the son-of-a-bitch.

555
01:11:43,702 --> 01:11:46,537
- He wants a meeting today.
- What did he say?

556
01:11:46,562 --> 01:11:50,892
What did he say... He wants us to send
Michael to hear the proposition.

557
01:11:51,293 --> 01:11:54,413
He promises that the deal
is too good to refuse.

558
01:11:54,840 --> 01:11:58,043
- And Bruno Tattaglia?
- That's part of the deal.

559
01:11:58,068 --> 01:12:02,362
- He cancels out what they did to Father.
- We should listen to them.

560
01:12:02,430 --> 01:12:05,514
No more! Not this time, Consigliere.

561
01:12:05,692 --> 01:12:09,215
No more meetings, discussions,
or Sollozzo tricks.

562
01:12:09,345 --> 01:12:12,430
I want Sollozzo, or we go to war...

563
01:12:12,455 --> 01:12:15,978
- The other families...
- They hand me Sollozzo!

564
01:12:16,505 --> 01:12:18,378
This is business, not personal!

565
01:12:18,403 --> 01:12:22,723
- They shot my father...
- Even that was business, not personal.

566
01:12:23,142 --> 01:12:26,926
Then business will have to suffer.
Do me a favour.

567
01:12:27,078 --> 01:12:30,834
No more advice on how to
patch things up. Just help me win.

568
01:12:37,550 --> 01:12:40,950
I found out about Captain McCluskey,
who broke Mike's jaw.

569
01:12:41,342 --> 01:12:44,767
He's definitely on Sollozzo's payroll,
and for big money.

570
01:12:45,724 --> 01:12:49,556
McCluskey has agreed to be
The Turk's bodyguard.

571
01:12:49,824 --> 01:12:53,238
So when Sollozzo is being guarded,
he's invulnerable.

572
01:12:53,688 --> 01:12:57,270
Nobody has ever gunned down
a New York police captain.

573
01:12:57,483 --> 01:13:03,038
All the families would come after you.
The Corleone family would be outcasts!

574
01:13:03,406 --> 01:13:06,585
Even the old man's political protection
would run for cover.

575
01:13:08,536 --> 01:13:12,422
Do me a favour.
Take this into consideration.

576
01:13:16,335 --> 01:13:17,930
All right, we'll wait.

577
01:13:23,342 --> 01:13:26,758
We can't wait. We can't wait.

578
01:13:27,763 --> 01:13:31,677
No matter what Sollozzo says,
he's going to kill Pop.

579
01:13:31,892 --> 01:13:34,979
That's the key for him.
We've got to get Sollozzo.

580
01:13:35,756 --> 01:13:39,884
- Mike is right.
- Let me ask you something.

581
01:13:40,233 --> 01:13:45,026
What about this McCluskey?
What do we do with this cop?

582
01:13:49,868 --> 01:13:52,333
They want to have a meeting
with me, right?

583
01:13:53,496 --> 01:13:58,408
It will be me, McCluskey and Sollozzo.

584
01:14:00,045 --> 01:14:01,588
Let's set the meeting.

585
01:14:04,206 --> 01:14:07,785
Get our informers to find out
where it's going to be held.

586
01:14:09,762 --> 01:14:13,630
We insist it's a public place.
A bar, a restaurant.

587
01:14:13,655 --> 01:14:17,367
Some place where there are people,
so I feel safe.

588
01:14:20,064 --> 01:14:23,018
They'll search me when I meet them,
right?

589
01:14:23,234 --> 01:14:26,105
So I can't have a weapon on me.

590
01:14:28,927 --> 01:14:34,101
But if Clemenza can figure out a way to
have a weapon planted there for me...

591
01:14:38,916 --> 01:14:40,576
...then I'll kill them both.

592
01:14:53,280 --> 01:14:57,989
Nice college boy. Didn't want to
get mixed up in the family business.

593
01:14:58,162 --> 01:15:01,696
Now you want to shoot a police captain
because he slapped you?

594
01:15:01,861 --> 01:15:08,279
This isn't like the army! You have to get
close and get their brains on your suit.

595
01:15:09,846 --> 01:15:11,528
You're taking this very personal.

596
01:15:11,553 --> 01:15:14,831
Tom, this is business
and he's taking it personal.

597
01:15:15,160 --> 01:15:18,969
- Where does it say you can't kill a cop?
- Come on, Mikey...

598
01:15:19,122 --> 01:15:25,576
I'm talking about a cop who's mixed
up in drugs, a dishonest cop.

599
01:15:25,796 --> 01:15:29,363
A cop who got mixed up in the rackets
and got what was coming.

600
01:15:30,230 --> 01:15:34,671
That's a terrific story. We have
newspaper people on the payroll, right?

601
01:15:36,195 --> 01:15:40,001
- They might like a story like that.
- They might.

602
01:15:43,646 --> 01:15:47,143
It's not personal, Sonny.
It's strictly business.

603
01:15:50,361 --> 01:15:55,358
It's as cold as they come. Impossible to
trace, so you don't worry about prints.

604
01:15:55,708 --> 01:16:00,133
I put a special tape on the trigger
and the butt. Try it.

605
01:16:12,039 --> 01:16:14,791
Is the trigger too tight?

606
01:16:17,493 --> 01:16:18,821
My ears!

607
01:16:18,846 --> 01:16:23,566
I left it noisy, so it scares away any
pain-in-the-ass innocent bystanders.

608
01:16:24,580 --> 01:16:27,293
You've shot them both.
Now what do you do?

609
01:16:29,637 --> 01:16:33,587
- Sit down, finish my dinner.
- Don't fool around.

610
01:16:33,612 --> 01:16:37,063
Let your hand drop to your side
and let the gun slip out.

611
01:16:37,282 --> 01:16:41,494
Everybody will still think you've got it.
They'll stare at your face,

612
01:16:41,663 --> 01:16:44,498
so walk out fast, but don't run.

613
01:16:44,748 --> 01:16:47,771
Don't look anybody in the eye,
but don't look away either.

614
01:16:48,283 --> 01:16:51,568
They'll be scared stiff,
so don't worry about nothing.

615
01:16:53,835 --> 01:16:55,836
You know, you're
gonna turn out be all right.

616
01:16:55,861 --> 01:16:58,153
You'll take a vacation,
nobody knows where,

617
01:16:58,178 --> 01:17:00,188
and we're gonna catch the hell.

618
01:17:00,840 --> 01:17:02,821
How bad do you think it will be?

619
01:17:02,955 --> 01:17:04,548
Pretty goddamn bad.

620
01:17:04,760 --> 01:17:07,644
Probably all the other families
will line up against us.

621
01:17:07,933 --> 01:17:08,626
That's alright.

622
01:17:08,651 --> 01:17:12,259
These things have to
happen every five, ten years.

623
01:17:12,284 --> 01:17:13,793
Helps gets rid of the bad blood.

624
01:17:13,818 --> 01:17:17,982
Been ten years since the last one.
You have to stop them at the beginning.

625
01:17:18,190 --> 01:17:20,476
Like they should have
stopped Hitler in Munich,

626
01:17:20,500 --> 01:17:22,234
They should've not letting
him get away with that.

627
01:17:22,259 --> 01:17:24,214
They were just asking for big trouble.

628
01:17:25,268 --> 01:17:29,231
You know, Mike, we were all proud
of you. Being a hero and all.

629
01:17:29,856 --> 01:17:31,368
Your father too.

630
01:18:09,576 --> 01:18:12,864
Nothing. Not a hint. Absolutely nothing.

631
01:18:13,961 --> 01:18:18,208
Even Sollozzo's people don't know
where the meeting will be held.

632
01:18:18,330 --> 01:18:19,813
How much time do we have?

633
01:18:21,510 --> 01:18:25,353
They're going to pick you up outside
Jack Dempsey's in an hour and a half.

634
01:18:27,390 --> 01:18:32,710
- We could put a tail on them.
- Sollozzo would lose our ass.

635
01:18:33,522 --> 01:18:38,100
- What about the negotiator?
- He's playing pinochle with my men.

636
01:18:38,318 --> 01:18:43,395
- He's happy. They're letting him win.
- Too risky. Maybe we should call it off.

637
01:18:43,527 --> 01:18:46,979
The negotiator plays cards
until Mike is back safe.

638
01:18:47,205 --> 01:18:50,823
- He could blast whoever is in the car.
- They'll expect that.

639
01:18:51,041 --> 01:18:53,492
Sollozzo might not even be
in the car, Sonny!

640
01:18:54,584 --> 01:18:56,707
I'll get it.

641
01:19:21,204 --> 01:19:23,280
Louis' restaurant in the Bronx.

642
01:19:23,446 --> 01:19:26,565
- Is it reliable?
- My man in McCluskey's precinct.

643
01:19:26,945 --> 01:19:32,269
A police captain is on call 24 hours
a day. He'll be there between 8 and 10.

644
01:19:32,747 --> 01:19:37,432
- Anybody know this joint?
- Sure, I do. It's perfect for us.

645
01:19:37,753 --> 01:19:42,747
A small family place, good food.
Everyone minds his business. Perfect.

646
01:19:43,350 --> 01:19:49,045
They've got an old-fashioned toilet.
You know, the box and the chain thing.

647
01:19:50,636 --> 01:19:53,177
We might be able to tape the gun
behind it.

648
01:19:53,648 --> 01:19:57,735
All right. Mike, you go to the restaurant,

649
01:19:58,039 --> 01:20:01,871
you eat, talk for a while, you relax.
Make them relax.

650
01:20:02,098 --> 01:20:07,092
Then you go to take a leak. No, better
still, you ask permission to go.

651
01:20:07,452 --> 01:20:12,161
Then you come back blasting.
Two shots in the head apiece.

652
01:20:12,327 --> 01:20:16,111
I want somebody very good
to plant that gun.

653
01:20:16,331 --> 01:20:19,332
I don't want him coming out
with just his dick in his hand.

654
01:20:19,728 --> 01:20:24,663
- The gun will be there.
- You drive him and pick him up after.

655
01:20:25,423 --> 01:20:27,914
Come on, let's move.

656
01:20:32,555 --> 01:20:35,640
Did he tell you to drop the gun
right away?

657
01:20:35,756 --> 01:20:37,998
Yeah, a million times.

658
01:20:42,397 --> 01:20:46,982
Don't forget. Two shots apiece in
the head as soon as you come out.

659
01:20:53,236 --> 01:20:55,922
How long do you think it will be
before I can come back?

660
01:20:57,455 --> 01:20:59,780
At least a year.

661
01:20:59,938 --> 01:21:04,692
I'll square it with Mom, that you're not
seeing her before you leave and...

662
01:21:06,088 --> 01:21:09,837
I'll get a message to that girlfriend
when the time is right.

663
01:21:16,054 --> 01:21:18,295
Take care.

664
01:21:20,311 --> 01:21:22,149
Take care, Mike.

665
01:21:54,779 --> 01:21:58,942
I'm glad you came. I hope we can
straighten everything out.

666
01:21:59,808 --> 01:22:04,553
It's not the way I wanted things to go.
It should never have happened.

667
01:22:04,937 --> 01:22:09,398
I want to straighten everything out.
I don't want my father bothered again.

668
01:22:09,423 --> 01:22:12,845
I swear on my children
that he won't be, Mike.

669
01:22:13,626 --> 01:22:16,051
But you have to keep an open mind
when we talk.

670
01:22:17,075 --> 01:22:21,532
I hope you're not a hothead like Sonny.
You can't talk business with him.

671
01:22:22,830 --> 01:22:25,238
He's a good kid.

672
01:22:28,917 --> 01:22:32,416
I'm sorry about the other night, Mike.

673
01:22:32,590 --> 01:22:37,484
I've got to frisk you, so turn around.
On your knees, facing me.

674
01:22:41,407 --> 01:22:46,483
I guess I'm getting too old for my job.
Too grouchy.

675
01:22:47,833 --> 01:22:51,616
Can't stand the aggravation.
You know how it is.

676
01:22:53,819 --> 01:22:55,717
He's clean.

677
01:23:22,025 --> 01:23:23,777
Going to Jersey?

678
01:23:26,643 --> 01:23:28,063
Maybe.

679
01:23:53,543 --> 01:23:55,747
Nice work, Lou.

680
01:24:32,526 --> 01:24:37,947
- How's the food in this restaurant?
- Try the veal. It's the best in the city.

681
01:24:37,972 --> 01:24:39,254
I'll have it.

682
01:25:15,251 --> 01:25:18,750
- I'm going to speak Italian to Mikey.
- Go ahead.

683
01:26:37,998 --> 01:26:40,667
What I want...

684
01:26:40,841 --> 01:26:43,379
What's most important to me...

685
01:26:45,630 --> 01:26:50,100
...is that I have a guarantee.
No more attempts on my father's life.

686
01:26:50,125 --> 01:26:54,508
What guarantees can I give you?
I'm the hunted one!

687
01:26:54,843 --> 01:26:58,077
I missed my chance.
You think too much of me, kid.

688
01:26:58,504 --> 01:27:00,474
I'm not that clever.

689
01:27:01,830 --> 01:27:04,096
All I want is a truce.

690
01:27:10,655 --> 01:27:14,630
I have to go to the bathroom.
Is it all right?

691
01:27:16,004 --> 01:27:18,201
When you got to go, you got to go.

692
01:27:24,052 --> 01:27:25,594
I frisked him. He's clean.

693
01:27:25,916 --> 01:27:28,005
Don't take too long.

694
01:27:31,050 --> 01:27:33,089
I've frisked a thousand punks.

695
01:32:23,587 --> 01:32:25,829
Okay, you take over.

696
01:32:42,815 --> 01:32:44,774
I love you, Grandpa.

697
01:32:47,361 --> 01:32:50,730
I'm sorry, Pa. He doesn't know you yet.

698
01:32:51,531 --> 01:32:54,616
- Hey, big guy. Give it to Grandpa.
- Okay.

699
01:32:54,826 --> 01:33:01,030
"I hope you get well, Grandpa, and wish
I see you soon. Your grandson Frank."

700
01:33:04,211 --> 01:33:06,333
Go with your mother.

701
01:33:06,546 --> 01:33:09,002
Take them downstairs.

702
01:33:14,721 --> 01:33:17,212
Go on, Carlo, you too.

703
01:33:18,433 --> 01:33:20,141
Go on.

704
01:33:40,628 --> 01:33:44,421
- What's the matter with you, Carlo?
- Shut up and set the table.

705
01:34:00,182 --> 01:34:06,552
Since McCluskey's killing, the police
have cracked down on our operations.

706
01:34:08,104 --> 01:34:13,023
And also the other families.
There's been a lot of bad blood.

707
01:34:13,237 --> 01:34:16,653
They hit us, so we hit them back.

708
01:34:17,157 --> 01:34:21,736
Through our newspaper contacts
we've been able to put out material

709
01:34:22,006 --> 01:34:26,253
about McCluskey's link with Sollozzo
in the drug rackets.

710
01:34:26,416 --> 01:34:28,575
So things are loosening up.

711
01:34:29,679 --> 01:34:37,306
And I sent Fredo to Las Vegas, under
the protection of Don Francesco of L.A.

712
01:34:37,427 --> 01:34:42,497
- I want him to rest.
- I'm going to learn the casino business.

713
01:34:49,439 --> 01:34:51,478
Where's Michael?

714
01:35:04,221 --> 01:35:06,907
It was Michael who killed Sollozzo.

715
01:35:09,042 --> 01:35:13,419
But he's safe. We're starting to work
to bring him back.

716
01:35:34,442 --> 01:35:39,068
Did you find out where that old pimp
Tattaglia is hiding? I want him now.

717
01:35:39,280 --> 01:35:42,364
Sonny, things are starting to loosen up.

718
01:35:42,575 --> 01:35:47,367
If you go after Tattaglia, all hell
will break loose. Pop can negotiate.

719
01:35:47,392 --> 01:35:53,519
- He must get better first. I'll decide...
- War is costly. We can't do business.

720
01:35:53,544 --> 01:35:57,564
- Neither can they. Don't worry about it!
- We can't afford a stalemate.

721
01:35:57,589 --> 01:36:02,547
- No more stalemate. I'll kill the bastard!
- You're getting a great reputation!

722
01:36:02,813 --> 01:36:07,926
Do as I say! If I had a Sicilian wartime
consigliere, I wouldn't be in this shape!

723
01:36:08,541 --> 01:36:10,406
Pop had Genco. Look what I got.

724
01:36:14,276 --> 01:36:16,268
I'm sorry. I didn't mean that.

725
01:36:17,859 --> 01:36:21,026
Ma made a little dinner. It's Sunday.

726
01:36:21,813 --> 01:36:26,309
Niggers are having a good time
with our policy banks in Harlem.

727
01:36:26,334 --> 01:36:29,704
Driving new Cadillacs,
paying 50 per cent on a bet.

728
01:36:30,449 --> 01:36:33,534
That's because they've started
making big money.

729
01:36:33,792 --> 01:36:36,205
Poppa never talked business
at the table.

730
01:36:37,387 --> 01:36:41,059
- Shut up, Connie...
- Don't you ever tell her to shut up.

731
01:36:42,091 --> 01:36:44,479
Don't interfere.

732
01:36:45,082 --> 01:36:49,449
I'd like to talk to you after dinner.
I could do more for the family...

733
01:36:49,474 --> 01:36:51,658
We don't discuss business at the table.

734
01:39:28,588 --> 01:39:32,289
Hey, hey, take me to the America, G.I.!

735
01:39:32,551 --> 01:39:36,251
Hey, hey, take me to the America, G.I.!
Clark Gable!

736
01:39:37,013 --> 01:39:42,553
America! Take me to the America, G.I.!
Clark Gable, Rita Hayworth!

737
01:42:36,481 --> 01:42:39,566
I apologise if I offended you.

738
01:42:39,776 --> 01:42:42,730
I'm a stranger in this country.

739
01:42:42,946 --> 01:42:46,362
I meant no disrespect
to you or your daughter.

740
01:42:51,535 --> 01:42:54,030
I'm an American, hiding in Sicily.

741
01:42:55,750 --> 01:42:58,585
My name is Michael Corleone.

742
01:43:00,129 --> 01:43:02,892
There are people who'd pay a lot
of money for that information.

743
01:43:06,395 --> 01:43:10,662
But then your daughter
would lose a father...

744
01:43:10,851 --> 01:43:13,072
...instead of gaining a husband.

745
01:43:21,605 --> 01:43:24,476
I want to meet your daughter.

746
01:43:24,501 --> 01:43:28,312
With your permission, and under
the supervision of your family.

747
01:43:29,808 --> 01:43:32,436
With all respect.

748
01:43:50,135 --> 01:43:51,221
Apollonia.

749
01:46:43,849 --> 01:46:46,423
I'll knock you dizzy.

750
01:46:51,774 --> 01:46:54,181
Save it for the library.

751
01:46:57,571 --> 01:47:00,358
We've got to pick up my sister.

752
01:47:18,216 --> 01:47:20,838
What's the matter?

753
01:47:22,471 --> 01:47:24,179
What's the matter?

754
01:47:26,038 --> 01:47:28,529
- It was my fault!
- Where is he?

755
01:47:28,643 --> 01:47:31,395
It was my fault. I hit him.

756
01:47:31,537 --> 01:47:36,080
I started a fight with him.
I hit him, so he hit me...

757
01:47:39,987 --> 01:47:43,522
I'm just going to get a doctor
to take a look at you.

758
01:47:43,547 --> 01:47:46,631
Sonny, please don't do anything.

759
01:47:47,346 --> 01:47:50,267
What's the matter with you?
What am I going to do?

760
01:47:50,292 --> 01:47:53,209
Make that baby an orphan
before he's born?

761
01:47:57,672 --> 01:48:00,673
You spic slobs still betting Yankees?

762
01:48:00,883 --> 01:48:04,217
Tell them to stop taking in action.

763
01:48:04,429 --> 01:48:06,468
We lost enough money last week.

764
01:48:13,312 --> 01:48:15,435
Come here, come here!

765
01:49:12,287 --> 01:49:15,490
If you touch my sister again,
I'll kill you.

766
01:53:09,079 --> 01:53:13,207
Hey! We weren't expecting you,
Kay. You should call.

767
01:53:13,290 --> 01:53:17,453
Yes, well I have. I mean,
I've tried writing and calling.

768
01:53:17,570 --> 01:53:21,318
- I want to reach Michael.
- Nobody knows where he is.

769
01:53:21,711 --> 01:53:24,491
We know that he's alright, but that's all.

770
01:53:26,831 --> 01:53:30,581
- What was that?
- An accident, but nobody was hurt.

771
01:53:31,580 --> 01:53:36,053
Tom, will you give this letter to Michael.
Please?

772
01:53:37,274 --> 01:53:42,196
If I accepted that, a court could prove
I have knowledge of his whereabouts.

773
01:53:43,397 --> 01:53:45,385
He'll get in touch with you.

774
01:53:45,410 --> 01:53:48,347
I let my cab go, so can I call
another one, please?

775
01:53:49,017 --> 01:53:50,467
Come on. Sorry.

776
01:54:10,474 --> 01:54:13,558
- Hello?
- Is Carlo there?

777
01:54:13,583 --> 01:54:15,908
- Who is this?
- A friend of Carlo.

778
01:54:16,127 --> 01:54:19,710
Tell him that I can't make it tonight
until later.

779
01:54:25,233 --> 01:54:27,107
Bitch!

780
01:54:28,890 --> 01:54:31,345
- Dinner's on the table.
- I'm not hungry.

781
01:54:31,438 --> 01:54:34,558
- The food is getting cold.
- I'll eat out later.

782
01:54:34,896 --> 01:54:37,268
You just told me to make you dinner!

783
01:54:45,687 --> 01:54:48,522
She has a filthy mouth, this Guinea brat.

784
01:54:52,738 --> 01:54:56,355
That's it, break it all, you spoiled
Guinea brat. Break it all!

785
01:55:06,146 --> 01:55:09,473
Why don't you bring your whore
home for dinner?

786
01:55:10,347 --> 01:55:12,632
Maybe I will.

787
01:55:18,666 --> 01:55:21,935
- Clean it up!
- Like hell I will!

788
01:55:21,960 --> 01:55:26,061
You skinny, spoiled brat.
Clean it up! Clean it up!

789
01:55:26,086 --> 01:55:29,918
Clean it up! I said, clean it up!
Clean it up!

790
01:55:32,619 --> 01:55:35,904
Clean it up. Clean that up, you...

791
01:55:38,686 --> 01:55:40,523
Clean it!

792
01:55:40,548 --> 01:55:44,938
Clean it up! Yeah, kill me.
Be a murderer, like your father!

793
01:55:44,963 --> 01:55:48,379
- All you Corleones are murderers!
- I hate you!

794
01:55:48,444 --> 01:55:51,279
Come on, kill me!

795
01:55:51,648 --> 01:55:53,308
Get out of here!

796
01:55:53,426 --> 01:55:56,629
- I hate you!
- Now I'll kill you.

797
01:55:56,893 --> 01:55:59,977
You Guinea brat. Get out of here!

798
01:56:09,947 --> 01:56:13,482
Connie, what's the matter?
I can't hear you.

799
01:56:14,076 --> 01:56:17,077
Connie, talk louder. The baby's crying.

800
01:56:17,288 --> 01:56:20,787
Santino, I can't understand.
I don't know.

801
01:56:21,417 --> 01:56:23,789
Yeah, Connie.

802
01:56:28,348 --> 01:56:30,387
You wait there.

803
01:56:32,553 --> 01:56:35,091
No, you just wait there.

804
01:56:37,380 --> 01:56:39,788
Son-of-a-bitch.

805
01:56:40,061 --> 01:56:43,097
- Son-of-a-bitch!
- What's the matter?

806
01:56:46,775 --> 01:56:50,358
Open the goddamn gate!
Get off your ass.

807
01:56:57,911 --> 01:56:59,571
Sonny!

808
01:57:05,883 --> 01:57:08,552
- Sonny.
- Get out of here!

809
01:57:08,868 --> 01:57:10,991
Go after him, go on!

810
01:57:40,286 --> 01:57:43,632
Son-of-a-bitch. Come on!

811
01:59:31,145 --> 01:59:32,824
Give me a drop.

812
01:59:41,322 --> 01:59:44,406
My wife is crying upstairs.

813
01:59:45,951 --> 01:59:49,201
I hear cars coming to the house.

814
01:59:53,000 --> 01:59:56,084
Consigliere of mine,

815
01:59:56,295 --> 01:59:59,664
I think you should tell your Don
what everyone seems to know.

816
01:59:59,882 --> 02:00:02,455
I didn't tell Mama anything.

817
02:00:03,245 --> 02:00:06,442
I was about to come up and wake you
and tell you.

818
02:00:09,887 --> 02:00:12,129
But you needed a drink first.

819
02:00:14,646 --> 02:00:16,389
Yeah.

820
02:00:18,900 --> 02:00:21,399
Well, now you've had your drink.

821
02:00:26,967 --> 02:00:31,183
They shot Sonny on the causeway.
He's dead.

822
02:00:48,388 --> 02:00:50,855
I want no inquiries made.

823
02:00:55,072 --> 02:00:57,348
I want no acts of vengeance.

824
02:00:59,148 --> 02:01:01,686
I want you to arrange a meeting...

825
02:01:02,944 --> 02:01:05,843
...with the heads of the five families.

826
02:01:07,633 --> 02:01:09,684
This war stops now.

827
02:01:31,555 --> 02:01:33,844
Call Bonasera.

828
02:01:34,099 --> 02:01:36,590
I need him now.

829
02:01:48,649 --> 02:01:53,356
This is Tom Hagen. I'm calling for
Vito Corleone, at his request.

830
02:01:53,928 --> 02:01:56,336
You owe your Don a service.

831
02:01:56,496 --> 02:01:59,912
He has no doubt that you will repay it.

832
02:02:00,125 --> 02:02:04,788
He will be at your funeral parlor
in one hour. Be there to greet him.

833
02:02:25,608 --> 02:02:30,305
Well, my friend, are you ready
to do me this service?

834
02:02:30,547 --> 02:02:34,270
Yes. What do you want me to do?

835
02:02:41,916 --> 02:02:46,745
I want you to use all your powers
and all your skills.

836
02:02:50,669 --> 02:02:53,542
I don't want his mother
to see him this way.

837
02:03:09,716 --> 02:03:12,440
Look how they massacred my boy.

838
02:04:45,237 --> 02:04:46,836
What's wrong?

839
02:05:27,568 --> 02:05:31,731
Are you driving yourself, Boss?
Is your wife coming with you?

840
02:05:31,874 --> 02:05:35,409
No, take her to her father's house
until things are safe.

841
02:05:35,628 --> 02:05:38,036
Okay, anything you say.

842
02:06:07,910 --> 02:06:10,365
Fabrizio!

843
02:06:22,216 --> 02:06:23,591
No, Apollonia!

844
02:06:46,865 --> 02:06:52,535
Don Barzini, I want to thank you
for helping me organize this meeting,

845
02:06:52,746 --> 02:06:57,952
and the other heads of the five families
from New York and New Jersey.

846
02:06:59,352 --> 02:07:02,436
Carmine Cuneo from the Bronx,

847
02:07:02,547 --> 02:07:06,082
and from Brooklyn...

848
02:07:07,588 --> 02:07:09,707
...Philip Tattaglia.

849
02:07:11,330 --> 02:07:13,671
And from Staten Island

850
02:07:14,188 --> 02:07:17,387
we have with us Victor Strachi.

851
02:07:17,895 --> 02:07:23,218
And the other associates that came as
far as from California and Kansas City

852
02:07:23,557 --> 02:07:27,637
and all the other territories
of the country. Thank you.

853
02:07:34,122 --> 02:07:37,175
How did things ever get so far?

854
02:07:37,687 --> 02:07:38,994
I don't know.

855
02:07:41,346 --> 02:07:45,331
It was so unfortunate, so unnecessary.

856
02:07:47,958 --> 02:07:51,604
Tattaglia lost a son, and I lost a son.

857
02:07:53,803 --> 02:07:57,397
We're quits. And if Tattaglia agrees,

858
02:07:57,422 --> 02:08:01,372
then I'm willing to let things go on
as before.

859
02:08:02,731 --> 02:08:06,025
We're grateful to Don Corleone
for calling this meeting.

860
02:08:06,526 --> 02:08:11,813
We all know him as a man of his word.
A modest man who listens to reason.

861
02:08:11,931 --> 02:08:15,845
Yes, Don Barzini. He's too modest.

862
02:08:16,181 --> 02:08:19,514
He had all the judges and politicians
in his pocket.

863
02:08:20,290 --> 02:08:22,738
He refused to share them.

864
02:08:23,518 --> 02:08:26,723
When did I ever refuse
an accommodation?

865
02:08:27,349 --> 02:08:29,189
All of you know me.

866
02:08:30,636 --> 02:08:35,801
When did I ever refuse,
except one time? And why?

867
02:08:37,489 --> 02:08:42,544
Because I believe this drug business
will destroy us in the years to come.

868
02:08:43,363 --> 02:08:47,686
It's not like gambling or liquor
or even women,

869
02:08:47,711 --> 02:08:53,522
which is something that most people
want, but is forbidden by the Church.

870
02:08:53,732 --> 02:08:58,594
Even the police that have helped us in
the past with gambling and other things

871
02:08:58,619 --> 02:09:02,664
will now refuse to help us
when it comes to narcotics.

872
02:09:02,873 --> 02:09:07,868
I believed that then...
and I believe that now.

873
02:09:08,126 --> 02:09:09,650
Times have changed.

874
02:09:10,381 --> 02:09:14,550
It's not like the old days,
when we could do anything we wanted.

875
02:09:15,160 --> 02:09:17,513
A refusal is not the act of a friend.

876
02:09:18,222 --> 02:09:23,730
If Don Corleone had all the judges and
politicians, then he must share them

877
02:09:23,755 --> 02:09:28,337
or let others use them. He must let us
draw the water from the well.

878
02:09:29,314 --> 02:09:32,341
Certainly he can present a bill
for such services.

879
02:09:33,056 --> 02:09:35,807
After all, we're not communists.

880
02:09:38,715 --> 02:09:41,345
I also don't believe in drugs.

881
02:09:41,970 --> 02:09:46,762
For years I paid my people extra, so
they wouldn't do that kind of business.

882
02:09:46,875 --> 02:09:49,959
Somebody says to them
"I have powders."

883
02:09:50,170 --> 02:09:56,874
"If you put up 3-4,000 dollar investment,
we can make 50,000 distributing."

884
02:09:57,583 --> 02:10:03,372
They can't resist. I want to control it
as a business, keep it respectable.

885
02:10:03,709 --> 02:10:07,792
I don't want it near schools,
I don't want it sold to children.

886
02:10:08,653 --> 02:10:10,473
That's an infámia.

887
02:10:11,649 --> 02:10:15,433
In my city we would keep the traffic
to the colored.

888
02:10:15,653 --> 02:10:18,738
They're animals,
so let them lose their souls.

889
02:10:25,480 --> 02:10:29,080
I hoped that we could come
here and reason together.

890
02:10:30,376 --> 02:10:37,423
And I'm willing to do whatever is
necessary to find a peaceful solution.

891
02:10:37,633 --> 02:10:42,129
We are agreed. The traffic in drugs
will be permitted, but controlled.

892
02:10:42,346 --> 02:10:46,723
Don Corleone will give us protection
in the east, and there will be peace.

893
02:10:46,934 --> 02:10:50,303
I must have strict assurance
from Corleone.

894
02:10:50,600 --> 02:10:54,052
As time goes by and his position
becomes stronger,

895
02:10:54,077 --> 02:10:56,532
will he attempt any individual vendetta?

896
02:10:56,779 --> 02:11:01,427
We are all reasonable men.
We don't have to give assurances.

897
02:11:02,241 --> 02:11:04,447
You talk about vengeance.

898
02:11:04,845 --> 02:11:07,551
Will vengeance bring your son
back to you?

899
02:11:08,139 --> 02:11:10,073
Or my boy to me?

900
02:11:10,935 --> 02:11:14,019
I forgo the vengeance of my son.

901
02:11:16,421 --> 02:11:19,422
But I have selfish reasons.

902
02:11:20,926 --> 02:11:24,921
My youngest son was forced
to leave this country...

903
02:11:26,389 --> 02:11:28,853
...because of this Sollozzo business.

904
02:11:29,601 --> 02:11:34,393
And I have to make arrangements
to bring him back here safely.

905
02:11:34,585 --> 02:11:36,974
Cleared of all these false charges.

906
02:11:38,693 --> 02:11:41,156
But I'm a superstitious man.

907
02:11:41,866 --> 02:11:47,927
If an unlucky accident should befall him,
if he should be shot by a police officer,

908
02:11:48,606 --> 02:11:52,057
or if he should hang himself
in his jail cell,

909
02:11:52,310 --> 02:11:55,003
or if he's struck by a bolt of lightning,

910
02:11:56,492 --> 02:11:59,595
then I'm going to blame
some of the people in this room.

911
02:12:01,653 --> 02:12:03,571
And that I do not forgive.

912
02:12:06,512 --> 02:12:08,680
But, that aside...

913
02:12:11,896 --> 02:12:14,402
...let me say that I swear...

914
02:12:15,907 --> 02:12:18,200
...on the souls of my grandchildren,

915
02:12:19,056 --> 02:12:23,188
that I will not be the one to break
the peace we've made here today.

916
02:12:48,994 --> 02:12:54,053
Should I insist that all of Tattaglia's
drug middlemen have clean records?

917
02:12:54,606 --> 02:12:56,931
Mention it. Don't insist.

918
02:12:58,841 --> 02:13:03,730
- Barzini will know without being told.
- You mean Tattaglia.

919
02:13:05,417 --> 02:13:10,838
Tattaglia's a pimp. He could never
have outfought Santino.

920
02:13:14,000 --> 02:13:19,727
But I didn't know until this day
that it was Barzini all along.

921
02:13:34,682 --> 02:13:36,841
Come on, Nancy.

922
02:13:38,061 --> 02:13:41,227
Keep together, everyone. Brian.

923
02:13:41,981 --> 02:13:44,187
Okay, all right.

924
02:13:57,104 --> 02:13:59,088
How long have you been back?

925
02:13:59,877 --> 02:14:01,728
I've been back a year.

926
02:14:03,169 --> 02:14:05,576
Longer than that, I think.

927
02:14:07,756 --> 02:14:10,212
It's good to see you, Kay.

928
02:14:21,141 --> 02:14:23,465
I'm working for my father now, Kay.

929
02:14:26,277 --> 02:14:29,555
He's been sick. Very sick.

930
02:14:30,799 --> 02:14:37,232
But you're not like him. You told me you
weren't going to become like your father.

931
02:14:38,599 --> 02:14:42,045
My father is no different
than any other powerful man.

932
02:14:42,980 --> 02:14:47,188
Any man who's responsible
for other people.

933
02:14:47,671 --> 02:14:49,877
Like a senator or president.

934
02:14:50,090 --> 02:14:52,545
- You know how naive you sound?
- Why?

935
02:14:52,759 --> 02:14:55,594
They don't have men killed.

936
02:14:58,619 --> 02:15:00,483
Who's being naive, Kay?

937
02:15:02,006 --> 02:15:07,166
My father's way of doing things is over.
Even he knows that.

938
02:15:07,698 --> 02:15:12,191
In five years the Corleone family
is going to be completely legitimate.

939
02:15:13,897 --> 02:15:18,207
Trust me. That's all I can tell you
about my business. Kay...

940
02:15:19,296 --> 02:15:22,702
Michael, why did you come here? Why?

941
02:15:23,857 --> 02:15:28,603
What do you want with me after all
this time? I've been calling and writing.

942
02:15:28,628 --> 02:15:32,269
I came because I need you.
I care for you.

943
02:15:32,294 --> 02:15:36,787
- Please stop it, Michael.
- Because... I want you to marry me.

944
02:15:38,100 --> 02:15:41,219
- It's too late.
- Please, Kay...

945
02:15:42,047 --> 02:15:46,259
I'll do anything you ask to make up for
what's happened to us.

946
02:15:47,980 --> 02:15:53,484
Because that's important, Kay.
Because what's important is that...

947
02:15:53,694 --> 02:15:58,190
...we have each other.
That we have a life together.

948
02:15:58,540 --> 02:16:01,304
That we have children. Our children.

949
02:16:02,870 --> 02:16:05,740
Kay, I need you.

950
02:16:07,079 --> 02:16:08,376
And I love you.

951
02:16:30,563 --> 02:16:34,312
Barzini's people chisel my territory
and we do nothing about it!

952
02:16:34,526 --> 02:16:38,109
- Soon I'll have no place to hang my hat!
- Be patient.

953
02:16:38,196 --> 02:16:41,280
I'm not asking for help.
Just take off the handcuffs.

954
02:16:41,483 --> 02:16:44,520
- Be patient.
- We've got to protect ourselves.

955
02:16:44,744 --> 02:16:48,113
- Let me recruit some new men.
- No.

956
02:16:48,331 --> 02:16:50,826
I don't want to give Barzini
an excuse to start fighting.

957
02:16:50,851 --> 02:16:52,344
Mike, you're wrong.

958
02:16:53,586 --> 02:16:55,246
Don Corleone...

959
02:16:55,763 --> 02:16:59,627
You once said that one day Tessio
and me could form our own family.

960
02:17:00,094 --> 02:17:03,905
Till today I would never think of it.
I must ask your permission.

961
02:17:04,946 --> 02:17:07,908
Michael is now head of the family.

962
02:17:07,933 --> 02:17:11,329
If he gives his permission,
then you have my blessing.

963
02:17:12,313 --> 02:17:14,506
After we make the move to Nevada

964
02:17:14,531 --> 02:17:17,636
you can take off from the Corleone
family and go on your own.

965
02:17:17,661 --> 02:17:19,190
After we make the move to Nevada.

966
02:17:19,215 --> 02:17:23,172
- How long will that be?
- Six months.

967
02:17:23,616 --> 02:17:29,701
Forgive me, but with you gone, me and
Pete will come under Barzini's thumb.

968
02:17:29,913 --> 02:17:35,370
I hate that Barzini. In six months' time
there will be nothing left to build on.

969
02:17:35,586 --> 02:17:38,586
- Do you have faith in my judgment?
- Yes.

970
02:17:38,702 --> 02:17:41,489
- Do I have your loyalty?
- Always, Godfather.

971
02:17:41,718 --> 02:17:45,134
Then be a friend to Michael.
Do as he says.

972
02:17:49,641 --> 02:17:54,970
Things are negotiated that'll solve your
problems and answer your questions.

973
02:17:55,313 --> 02:17:58,231
That's all I can tell you now.

974
02:17:58,441 --> 02:18:00,730
Carlo, you grew up in Nevada.

975
02:18:01,137 --> 02:18:03,878
When we make our move there,
you'll be my right-hand man.

976
02:18:04,531 --> 02:18:08,822
Tom Hagen is no longer consigliere.
He'll be our lawyer in Vegas.

977
02:18:09,497 --> 02:18:12,948
That's no reflection on Tom,
just how I want it.

978
02:18:13,200 --> 02:18:16,083
If I ever need help, who's a better
consigliere than my father?

979
02:18:16,108 --> 02:18:17,177
That's it.

980
02:18:36,312 --> 02:18:39,847
- Thank you, Poppa.
- I'm happy for you, Carlo.

981
02:18:40,616 --> 02:18:43,771
Mike... Why am I out?

982
02:18:45,071 --> 02:18:47,658
You're not a wartime consigliere, Tom.

983
02:18:49,162 --> 02:18:51,595
Things may get rough with the move.

984
02:18:52,464 --> 02:18:53,681
Tom.

985
02:18:58,834 --> 02:19:03,994
I advised Michael. I never thought
you were a bad consigliere.

986
02:19:04,214 --> 02:19:09,325
I thought Santino was a
bad Don, rest in peace.

987
02:19:09,803 --> 02:19:13,389
Michael has all my confidence,
just as you do.

988
02:19:14,079 --> 02:19:19,373
But there are reasons why you must
have no part in what is going to happen.

989
02:19:19,927 --> 02:19:22,967
- Maybe I could help.
- You're out, Tom.

990
02:20:12,281 --> 02:20:16,493
I can't get over the way your face looks.
So good!

991
02:20:16,715 --> 02:20:19,555
This doctor did some job.
Did Kay talk you into it?

992
02:20:19,580 --> 02:20:21,089
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Hey, wait, hey!

993
02:20:21,367 --> 02:20:24,935
Leave them out here.
He's tired and wants to clean up.

994
02:20:24,960 --> 02:20:27,451
Let me open the door, all right?

995
02:20:34,053 --> 02:20:39,758
- Hello, Mike! Welcome to Las Vegas!
- All for you, kid! It's all his idea.

996
02:20:39,975 --> 02:20:42,727
- Your brother Freddy.
- Girls?

997
02:20:46,217 --> 02:20:49,631
I'll be right back. Keep them occupied.

998
02:20:50,480 --> 02:20:54,247
- Anything you want, kid, anything.
- Who are the girls?

999
02:20:55,285 --> 02:20:58,891
- That's for you to find out.
- Get rid of them, Fredo.

1000
02:21:00,245 --> 02:21:04,100
- Hey, Mike...
- I'm here on business. Get rid of them.

1001
02:21:05,098 --> 02:21:08,383
I'm tired. Get rid of the band too.

1002
02:21:13,592 --> 02:21:16,676
Hey, take off. Take off. Let's go.

1003
02:21:17,053 --> 02:21:19,975
Hey, that's it. Hey, Angelo.

1004
02:21:20,865 --> 02:21:22,934
Hey, come on! Scram!

1005
02:21:24,561 --> 02:21:29,021
Come on, honey. I don't know
what's the matter with him, Johnny.

1006
02:21:29,644 --> 02:21:31,165
Sorry.

1007
02:21:31,512 --> 02:21:34,217
I don't know. He's tired.

1008
02:21:41,077 --> 02:21:43,050
What happened to Moe Greene?

1009
02:21:44,151 --> 02:21:48,203
He had some business. He said to
give him a call when the party started.

1010
02:21:48,793 --> 02:21:51,118
Well, give him a call.

1011
02:21:51,963 --> 02:21:55,296
- Johnny, how are you?
- Nice to see you, Mike.

1012
02:21:55,480 --> 02:21:57,520
- We're proud of you.
- Thanks.

1013
02:21:57,579 --> 02:22:01,074
Sit down, I want to talk to you.
The Don is proud too.

1014
02:22:01,322 --> 02:22:03,817
Well, I owe it all to him.

1015
02:22:04,314 --> 02:22:06,335
He knows how grateful you are.

1016
02:22:06,360 --> 02:22:08,800
That's why...
he'd like to ask a favour of you.

1017
02:22:09,605 --> 02:22:10,957
Mike, what can I do?

1018
02:22:12,650 --> 02:22:18,329
We're thinking of giving up our interests
in the olive oil business and settle here.

1019
02:22:19,010 --> 02:22:22,298
Now Moe Green will sell us his share
of the casino and the hotel,

1020
02:22:22,331 --> 02:22:25,042
so it can be completely
owned by family. Tom!

1021
02:22:25,067 --> 02:22:27,231
Mike, are you sure about that?

1022
02:22:27,256 --> 02:22:30,036
Moe loves the business. He never
said nothing to me about selling.

1023
02:22:30,236 --> 02:22:32,700
I'll make him an offer he can't refuse.

1024
02:22:34,400 --> 02:22:36,303
See, Johnny...

1025
02:22:36,828 --> 02:22:39,343
See, we figure that entertainment
will be a big factor

1026
02:22:39,368 --> 02:22:40,867
in drawing gamblers to the casino.

1027
02:22:41,189 --> 02:22:44,481
We hope you'll sign a contract
to appear five times a year.

1028
02:22:47,847 --> 02:22:52,276
Perhaps convince some of your friends
in the movies to do the same.

1029
02:22:53,648 --> 02:22:55,207
We're counting on you.

1030
02:22:57,894 --> 02:22:58,660
Sure, Mike.

1031
02:22:59,220 --> 02:23:01,467
I'll do anything for my godfather.
You know that.

1032
02:23:01,906 --> 02:23:03,140
Good.

1033
02:23:04,659 --> 02:23:09,202
Hey, Mike! Hello, fellows.
Everybody's here. Freddy, Tom.

1034
02:23:09,473 --> 02:23:11,512
- Good to see you.
- How are you, Moe?

1035
02:23:11,666 --> 02:23:16,826
Have everything? Specially prepared
food, the best dancers, and good credit.

1036
02:23:17,046 --> 02:23:20,133
Draw chips for everybody,
so they can play on the house.

1037
02:23:23,341 --> 02:23:26,253
Is my credit good enough
to buy you out?

1038
02:23:27,761 --> 02:23:29,136
Buy me out?

1039
02:23:29,705 --> 02:23:34,694
The casino, the hotel. The
Corleone family wants to buy you out.

1040
02:23:35,521 --> 02:23:38,116
The Corleone family
wants to buy me out?

1041
02:23:38,311 --> 02:23:40,735
No, I buy you out.
You don't buy me out.

1042
02:23:40,945 --> 02:23:44,029
Your casino loses money.
We can do better.

1043
02:23:44,348 --> 02:23:48,453
- You think I'm skimming off the top?
- You're unlucky.

1044
02:23:53,253 --> 02:23:55,504
You goddamn Guineas
really make me laugh.

1045
02:23:55,725 --> 02:23:58,687
I do you a favor and take Freddy here in
when you're having a bad time,

1046
02:23:58,712 --> 02:24:00,418
and now you try to push me out!

1047
02:24:01,609 --> 02:24:05,319
You took Freddy in because the Corleone
family bankrolled your casino

1048
02:24:05,344 --> 02:24:08,525
because the Molinari family honor
code guaranteed his safety.

1049
02:24:08,550 --> 02:24:10,493
Now let's talk business.

1050
02:24:10,557 --> 02:24:11,700
Yes, let's talk business, Mike.

1051
02:24:12,081 --> 02:24:13,447
First of all, you're all done.

1052
02:24:13,472 --> 02:24:15,717
The Corleone family don't even
have that kind of muscle anymore.

1053
02:24:15,937 --> 02:24:17,401
The Godfather is sick, right?

1054
02:24:17,426 --> 02:24:20,194
You're getting chased out of New York
by Barzini and the other famillies.

1055
02:24:20,349 --> 02:24:21,737
What do you think is going on here?

1056
02:24:21,762 --> 02:24:23,983
You think you can come to
my hotel and take over?

1057
02:24:24,404 --> 02:24:28,951
I talked to Barzini. I can make a deal
with him and still keep my hotel!

1058
02:24:29,534 --> 02:24:32,315
Is that why you slapped my brother
around in public?

1059
02:24:33,121 --> 02:24:37,866
That was nothing, Mike.
Moe didn't mean nothing by that.

1060
02:24:37,990 --> 02:24:40,285
He flies off the
handle once in awhile,

1061
02:24:40,309 --> 02:24:42,301
but Moe and me are good friends.
Right, Moe, huh?

1062
02:24:42,422 --> 02:24:43,640
I've got a business to run.

1063
02:24:44,266 --> 02:24:46,918
I've got to kick asses
sometimes to make it run right.

1064
02:24:47,135 --> 02:24:50,123
We had a little argument, Freddy and I,
so I had to straighten him out.

1065
02:24:51,222 --> 02:24:53,235
You straightened my brother out?

1066
02:24:54,001 --> 02:24:56,798
He was banging cocktail
waitresses, two at a time!

1067
02:24:56,823 --> 02:24:58,621
Players couldn't get
a drink at the table.

1068
02:24:58,646 --> 02:25:00,042
What's wrong with you?

1069
02:25:05,262 --> 02:25:09,094
I leave for New York tomorrow.
Think about a price.

1070
02:25:09,552 --> 02:25:11,047
Son-of-a-bitch!

1071
02:25:11,072 --> 02:25:13,895
Do you know who I am?
I'm Moe Greene!

1072
02:25:13,920 --> 02:25:16,514
I made my bones when you
were out with cheerleaders.

1073
02:25:16,539 --> 02:25:19,872
Wait a minute, Moe. I have an idea.

1074
02:25:20,084 --> 02:25:23,583
Tom, you're the consigliere.
Talk to the Don...

1075
02:25:23,748 --> 02:25:28,641
Just a minute. Don is semi-retired and
Mike is in charge of the family business.

1076
02:25:29,143 --> 02:25:32,076
If you have anything to say,
say it to Michael.

1077
02:25:36,246 --> 02:25:41,205
Mike, you don't come to Las Vegas and
talk to a man like Moe Greene like that!

1078
02:25:43,023 --> 02:25:44,258
Fredo...

1079
02:25:45,408 --> 02:25:47,759
You're my older brother, and I love you.

1080
02:25:49,677 --> 02:25:52,995
But don't ever take sides with
anyone against the family again.

1081
02:26:04,210 --> 02:26:08,837
I have to see my father and his people,
so have dinner without me.

1082
02:26:10,251 --> 02:26:11,737
This weekend we'll go out.

1083
02:26:11,762 --> 02:26:15,238
We'll go to the city, we'll see a show,
 and we'll have dinner.

1084
02:26:22,302 --> 02:26:25,303
Oh, Michael. Your sister wants
to ask you something.

1085
02:26:25,613 --> 02:26:27,772
- Let her ask.
- She's afraid to.

1086
02:26:27,844 --> 02:26:30,514
They want you to be godfather
to their boy.

1087
02:26:30,736 --> 02:26:32,776
- We'll see.
- Will you?

1088
02:26:32,929 --> 02:26:35,384
Let me think about it. Come on.

1089
02:26:43,882 --> 02:26:46,545
Barzini will move against you first.

1090
02:26:46,863 --> 02:26:50,882
He'll set up a meeting with someone
you absolutely trust.

1091
02:26:51,458 --> 02:26:53,661
Guaranteeing your safety.

1092
02:26:54,601 --> 02:26:57,506
And at that meeting
you'll be assassinated.

1093
02:27:02,518 --> 02:27:05,553
I like to drink wine more than I used to.

1094
02:27:06,905 --> 02:27:08,999
Anyway, I'm drinking more.

1095
02:27:09,024 --> 02:27:10,738
It's good for you, Pop.

1096
02:27:15,530 --> 02:27:16,911
I don't know.

1097
02:27:18,931 --> 02:27:21,854
Your wife and children,
Are you happy with them?

1098
02:27:22,913 --> 02:27:26,120
- Very happy.
- That's good.

1099
02:27:27,498 --> 02:27:32,245
I hope you don't mind the way I keep
going over this Barzini business.

1100
02:27:32,657 --> 02:27:34,284
No, not at all.

1101
02:27:34,565 --> 02:27:36,161
It's an old habit.

1102
02:27:36,929 --> 02:27:39,976
I spend my life trying not to be careless.

1103
02:27:41,540 --> 02:27:44,483
Women and children can
be careless, but not men.

1104
02:27:48,297 --> 02:27:50,622
- How's your boy?
- He's good.

1105
02:27:50,801 --> 02:27:53,755
You know he looks more
like you every day.

1106
02:27:56,252 --> 02:27:57,850
He's smarter than I am.

1107
02:27:58,733 --> 02:28:01,590
He's three years old and can
read the funny papers.

1108
02:28:02,789 --> 02:28:04,496
Read the funny papers.

1109
02:28:11,944 --> 02:28:17,885
I want you to arrange for a telephone
man to check all in- and out-going calls.

1110
02:28:17,910 --> 02:28:21,265
I did it already.
I took care of that, Pop.

1111
02:28:21,289 --> 02:28:23,678
That's right. I forgot.

1112
02:28:27,254 --> 02:28:28,494
What's the matter?

1113
02:28:29,854 --> 02:28:31,274
What's bothering you?

1114
02:28:35,449 --> 02:28:36,623
I'll handle it.

1115
02:28:37,783 --> 02:28:40,463
I told you I can handle it,
so I'll handle it.

1116
02:28:53,331 --> 02:28:56,992
I knew that Santino would
have to go through all this.

1117
02:28:57,821 --> 02:28:59,969
And Fredo...

1118
02:29:02,136 --> 02:29:04,209
Fredo was, well...

1119
02:29:06,153 --> 02:29:09,212
But I never wanted this for you.

1120
02:29:11,177 --> 02:29:12,776
I worked my whole life.

1121
02:29:12,801 --> 02:29:16,012
I don't have to apologise for
taking care of my family.

1122
02:29:16,447 --> 02:29:20,288
And I refused to be a fool,

1123
02:29:20,313 --> 02:29:24,233
dancing on a string held
by all those big shots.

1124
02:29:26,463 --> 02:29:30,591
I don't apologise. That's my life,
but I thought that...

1125
02:29:31,692 --> 02:29:33,970
that when it was your time, that...

1126
02:29:34,400 --> 02:29:37,217
that you would be the one
to hold the strings.

1127
02:29:38,556 --> 02:29:41,233
Senator Corleone.

1128
02:29:42,176 --> 02:29:44,278
Governor Corleone. Something.

1129
02:29:44,349 --> 02:29:46,756
Another pezzo da novanta.

1130
02:29:47,346 --> 02:29:48,805
Well...

1131
02:29:52,246 --> 02:29:56,205
Just wasn't enough time, Michael.
Wasn't enough time.

1132
02:29:56,263 --> 02:30:00,095
We'll get there, Pop. We'll get there.

1133
02:30:04,446 --> 02:30:08,528
Now listen, whoever comes to you
with this Barzini meeting,

1134
02:30:09,135 --> 02:30:12,215
he's the traitor. Don't forget that.

1135
02:30:29,142 --> 02:30:31,095
Can I hold it, please?

1136
02:30:46,452 --> 02:30:49,980
- Can I water these?
- Yes, go ahead.

1137
02:30:50,639 --> 02:30:53,533
Over here, over here.

1138
02:30:55,063 --> 02:30:58,227
Be careful. You're spilling it.

1139
02:31:03,869 --> 02:31:05,753
Antony!

1140
02:31:05,778 --> 02:31:07,854
Come here, come here.

1141
02:31:11,721 --> 02:31:14,556
That's it. We'll put it right there.

1142
02:31:20,396 --> 02:31:23,682
I'll show you something. Come here.

1143
02:31:25,042 --> 02:31:27,082
Stand there.

1144
02:31:30,579 --> 02:31:33,070
Give me an orange!

1145
02:31:50,886 --> 02:31:52,962
That's a new trick.

1146
02:31:53,701 --> 02:31:56,702
You run in there. Run in there.

1147
02:32:09,370 --> 02:32:11,695
Where are you?

1148
02:35:09,134 --> 02:35:10,880
Mike, can I have a minute?

1149
02:35:21,574 --> 02:35:23,934
Barzini wants to arrange a meeting.

1150
02:35:24,087 --> 02:35:27,004
He says we can straighten out
any of our problems.

1151
02:35:28,191 --> 02:35:30,063
- You talked to him?
- Yeah.

1152
02:35:31,674 --> 02:35:35,670
I can arrange security. On my territory.

1153
02:35:38,415 --> 02:35:41,535
- All right?
- All right.

1154
02:35:58,687 --> 02:36:00,761
Do you know how they're
going to come at you?

1155
02:36:04,105 --> 02:36:06,518
They're arranging a
meeting in Brooklyn.

1156
02:36:06,543 --> 02:36:07,730
Tessio's ground.

1157
02:36:09,886 --> 02:36:11,635
Where I'll be safe.

1158
02:36:23,991 --> 02:36:26,942
I always thought it would be
Clemenza, not Tessio.

1159
02:36:27,721 --> 02:36:31,575
It's the smart move.
Tessio was always smarter.

1160
02:36:33,749 --> 02:36:35,825
But I'm going to wait.

1161
02:36:36,290 --> 02:36:38,579
After the baptism.

1162
02:36:40,442 --> 02:36:43,129
I've decided to be godfather
to Connie's baby.

1163
02:36:44,502 --> 02:36:47,167
And then I'll meet with Don Barzini

1164
02:36:47,384 --> 02:36:52,107
and Tattaglia.
All the heads of the five families.

1165
02:39:13,945 --> 02:39:16,851
Michael, do you believe in God,
the Father Almighty,

1166
02:39:16,876 --> 02:39:18,658
Creator of Heaven and Earth?

1167
02:39:19,003 --> 02:39:19,926
I do.

1168
02:39:19,951 --> 02:39:23,320
Do you believe in Jesus Christ,
His only Son, our Lord?

1169
02:39:23,757 --> 02:39:24,775
I do.

1170
02:39:24,800 --> 02:39:28,715
Do you believe in the Holy Ghost,
the Holy Catholic Church?

1171
02:39:29,156 --> 02:39:30,485
I do.

1172
02:40:35,872 --> 02:40:40,111
Michael Francis Rizzi,
do you renounce Satan?

1173
02:40:46,521 --> 02:40:48,021
I do renounce him.

1174
02:40:57,616 --> 02:40:59,075
And all his works?

1175
02:41:12,394 --> 02:41:13,972
I do renounce them.

1176
02:41:15,482 --> 02:41:17,024
Oh, God!

1177
02:41:19,632 --> 02:41:23,380
- And all his pomps?
- I do renounce them.

1178
02:41:39,196 --> 02:41:42,980
Michael Rizzi,
will you be baptized?

1179
02:41:43,371 --> 02:41:44,561
I will.

1180
02:41:51,516 --> 02:41:57,804
Michael Rizzi, go in peace, and may
the Lord be with you. Amen.

1181
02:42:11,163 --> 02:42:13,203
Kay!

1182
02:42:13,329 --> 02:42:15,405
Kiss your godfather.

1183
02:42:39,841 --> 02:42:43,219
Carlo. I can't go to Vegas.

1184
02:42:43,252 --> 02:42:45,836
Something's come up.
Everybody has to leave without us.

1185
02:42:45,861 --> 02:42:48,903
- Mike, it's our first vacation!
- Connie, please.

1186
02:42:49,141 --> 02:42:53,269
Go back to the house, wait for my call.
It's important.

1187
02:42:53,452 --> 02:42:55,824
I'll only be a couple of days.

1188
02:43:12,286 --> 02:43:14,814
We're on our way to Brooklyn.

1189
02:43:16,180 --> 02:43:20,529
- I hope Mike can get us a good deal.
- I'm sure he will.

1190
02:43:28,170 --> 02:43:33,116
Sal, Tom, the boss says he'll come in a
separate car, so you two go on ahead.

1191
02:43:33,620 --> 02:43:37,282
- That screws up my arrangements.
- That's what he said.

1192
02:43:37,307 --> 02:43:38,760
I can't go either, Sal.

1193
02:43:51,292 --> 02:43:55,839
Tell Mike it was only business.
I always liked him.

1194
02:43:56,992 --> 02:43:59,729
- He understands that.
- Excuse me, Sal.

1195
02:44:05,886 --> 02:44:08,206
Tom, can you get me off the hook?

1196
02:44:09,320 --> 02:44:12,347
- For old times' sake?
- Can't do it, Sally.

1197
02:44:57,995 --> 02:45:00,404
You have to answer for Santino, Carlo.

1198
02:45:05,665 --> 02:45:10,292
- Mike, you got it all wrong.
- You fingered Sonny for Barzini.

1199
02:45:10,503 --> 02:45:13,612
That little farce you played
with my sister.

1200
02:45:14,551 --> 02:45:16,447
You think that could
fool a Corleone?

1201
02:45:16,472 --> 02:45:19,207
I'm innocent. I swear on the kids.

1202
02:45:19,794 --> 02:45:22,371
- Please, don't do this.
- Sit down.

1203
02:45:25,200 --> 02:45:27,690
Don't do this to me, please.

1204
02:45:36,697 --> 02:45:38,396
Barzini is dead.

1205
02:45:40,478 --> 02:45:42,443
So is Philip Tattaglia.

1206
02:45:44,105 --> 02:45:45,613
Moe Greene.

1207
02:45:46,485 --> 02:45:50,701
Strachi. Cuneo.

1208
02:45:52,263 --> 02:45:56,522
Today I settle all family business,
so don't tell me you're innocent, Carlo.

1209
02:45:57,584 --> 02:45:59,268
Admit what you did.

1210
02:46:03,203 --> 02:46:04,609
Get him a drink.

1211
02:46:11,101 --> 02:46:12,861
Come on.

1212
02:46:13,863 --> 02:46:15,488
Don't be afraid, Carlo.

1213
02:46:16,418 --> 02:46:19,893
Come on, do you think I'd
make my sister a widow?

1214
02:46:20,418 --> 02:46:23,051
I'm godfather to your son, Carlo.

1215
02:46:30,003 --> 02:46:32,577
Go ahead, drink, drink.

1216
02:46:36,979 --> 02:46:40,726
No, you're out of the family business.
That's your punishment.

1217
02:46:41,808 --> 02:46:45,415
You're finished.
I'm putting you on a plane to Vegas.

1218
02:46:45,912 --> 02:46:47,047
Tom.

1219
02:46:51,626 --> 02:46:54,436
I want you to stay there. Understand?

1220
02:46:55,346 --> 02:46:57,741
Only don't tell me you're innocent.

1221
02:46:59,278 --> 02:47:03,896
Because it insults my intelligence.
Makes me very angry.

1222
02:47:07,728 --> 02:47:09,942
Who approached you?

1223
02:47:10,972 --> 02:47:13,499
Tattaglia or Barzini?

1224
02:47:21,177 --> 02:47:23,338
It was Barzini.

1225
02:47:26,890 --> 02:47:28,780
Good.

1226
02:47:34,733 --> 02:47:38,362
There's a car waiting outside
to take you to the airport.

1227
02:47:38,929 --> 02:47:41,588
I'll call your wife and tell her
what flight you're on.

1228
02:47:47,392 --> 02:47:49,901
- Mike...
- Get out of my sight.

1229
02:48:15,515 --> 02:48:16,926
Hello, Carlo.

1230
02:49:15,384 --> 02:49:19,797
- I'm trying to tell you...
- Mama, please!

1231
02:49:28,549 --> 02:49:29,842
Michael!

1232
02:49:30,604 --> 02:49:33,507
- What is it?
- Where is he?

1233
02:49:35,041 --> 02:49:39,778
Michael, you lousy bastard!
You killed my husband.

1234
02:49:40,184 --> 02:49:44,010
You waited until Papa died,
so nobody could stop you.

1235
02:49:44,416 --> 02:49:47,687
You blamed him for Sonny.
You always did, everybody did.

1236
02:49:47,712 --> 02:49:53,192
But you never thought about me!
Now what are we going to do?

1237
02:49:53,520 --> 02:49:55,228
Connie.

1238
02:49:57,444 --> 02:50:00,074
Why do you think he kept
Carlo at the Mall?

1239
02:50:00,174 --> 02:50:02,617
All the time, he knew
he was going to kill him.

1240
02:50:02,965 --> 02:50:05,942
And you stood
godfather to our baby.

1241
02:50:05,967 --> 02:50:08,249
You lousy cold-hearted bastard!

1242
02:50:08,546 --> 02:50:12,746
Want to know how many men he had
killed with Carlo? Read the papers!

1243
02:50:12,771 --> 02:50:16,040
That's your husband,
that's your husband!

1244
02:50:24,937 --> 02:50:28,769
No! No, no...

1245
02:50:28,923 --> 02:50:32,588
Take her upstairs. Get her a doctor.

1246
02:50:53,747 --> 02:50:55,656
She's hysterical.

1247
02:51:00,314 --> 02:51:01,724
Hysterical.

1248
02:51:03,809 --> 02:51:06,478
Michael, is it true?

1249
02:51:07,549 --> 02:51:11,167
- Don't ask me about my business, Kay.
- Is it true?

1250
02:51:11,319 --> 02:51:14,615
Don't ask me about my business.
Enough!

1251
02:51:34,023 --> 02:51:35,814
All right.

1252
02:51:38,420 --> 02:51:40,171
This one time.

1253
02:51:44,185 --> 02:51:47,831
This one time I'll let you
ask me about my affairs.

1254
02:51:53,399 --> 02:51:56,234
Is it true?

1255
02:51:59,072 --> 02:52:00,898
Is it?

1256
02:52:02,408 --> 02:52:03,902
No.

1257
02:52:17,590 --> 02:52:20,875
I guess we both need a drink.
Come on.

1258
02:52:51,711 --> 02:52:54,119
Don Corleone.

